window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-24-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 24 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000074881","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"If 8 &#8594; 64, 9 &#8594; 81, 10 &#8594; 100, then 12 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 8 &#8594; 64, 9 &#8594; 81, 10 &#8594; 100, तो 12 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"120"},"2":{"en":"132"},"3":{"en":"156"},"4":{"en":"144"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Each number is written as its own square: 8² = 64, 9² = 81 and 10² = 100<br>So 12 is written as 12² = 144<br>Hence the missing number is 144<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 144.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक संख्या को उसके वर्ग के रूप में लिखा जाता है: 8² = 64, 9² = 81 तथा 10² = 100<br>अतः 12 को 12² = 144 के रूप में लिखा जाएगा<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 144 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 144 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000074882","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The average weight of 10 men is increased by 2 kg when one of the men who weighs 60 kg is replaced by a new man. What is the weight of the new man? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जब 60 किग्रा भार वाले एक व्यक्ति के स्थान पर एक नया व्यक्ति आता है तो 10 व्यक्तियों का औसत भार 2 किग्रा बढ़ जाता है। नए व्यक्ति का भार क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70 kg","hi":"70 किग्रा"},"2":{"en":"80 kg","hi":"80 किग्रा"},"3":{"en":"48 kg","hi":"48 किग्रा"},"4":{"en":"32 kg","hi":"32 किग्रा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The average of 10 men rises by 2 kg, so the total weight rises by 10 × 2 = 20 kg<br>The new man must therefore weigh 60 + 20 = 80 kg<br>Hence the weight of the new man is 80 kg<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 80 kg.</b>","hi":"10 व्यक्तियों का औसत 2 किग्रा बढ़ता है, अतः कुल भार 10 × 2 = 20 किग्रा बढ़ता है<br>इसलिए नए व्यक्ति का भार 60 + 20 = 80 किग्रा होना चाहिए<br>अतः नए व्यक्ति का भार 80 किग्रा है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 80 किग्रा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000074883","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What comes next?<br>3, 7, 15, 31, 63, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आगे क्या आएगा?<br>3, 7, 15, 31, 63, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"127"},"2":{"en":"125"},"3":{"en":"126"},"4":{"en":"121"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each term is obtained by doubling the previous term and adding 1: 3 × 2 + 1 = 7, 7 × 2 + 1 = 15, 15 × 2 + 1 = 31 and 31 × 2 + 1 = 63<br>Next term = 63 × 2 + 1 = 127<br>So the next number is 127<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 127.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद पिछले पद का दुगुना करके 1 जोड़ने से मिलता है: 3 × 2 + 1 = 7, 7 × 2 + 1 = 15, 15 × 2 + 1 = 31 तथा 31 × 2 + 1 = 63<br>अगला पद = 63 × 2 + 1 = 127<br>अतः अगली संख्या 127 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 127 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000074884","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Some engineers are doctors. No doctor is a teacher.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some engineers are not teachers.<br>II. All engineers are teachers. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह निष्कर्ष पहचानिए जो निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कुछ इंजीनियर डॉक्टर हैं। कोई डॉक्टर शिक्षक नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ इंजीनियर शिक्षक नहीं हैं।<br>II. सभी इंजीनियर शिक्षक हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Some engineers are doctors and no doctor is a teacher, so those engineers who are doctors can never be teachers<br>That gives some engineers who are not teachers, so I follows<br>The second conclusion says every engineer is a teacher, which is the opposite of what the statements show, so II does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"कुछ इंजीनियर डॉक्टर हैं और कोई डॉक्टर शिक्षक नहीं है, अतः जो इंजीनियर डॉक्टर हैं वे कभी शिक्षक नहीं हो सकते<br>इससे कुछ इंजीनियर शिक्षक नहीं हैं, अतः I निकलता है<br>दूसरा निष्कर्ष कहता है कि सभी इंजीनियर शिक्षक हैं, जो कथनों के विपरीत है, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000074885","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"Three statements are given, followed by three conclusions numbered I, II, and III. Assuming the statements to be true, even if they seem to be at variance with commonly known facts, decide which of the conclusions logically follow(s) from the statements.<br><b>Statements:</b><br>All Deal is Close.<br>Some Close is Cross.<br>No Deal is Drive.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some Close is not Drive.<br>II. All Cross is Close.<br>III. Some Deal is Cross. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तीन कथन और उनके बाद I, II तथा III क्रमांकित तीन निष्कर्ष दिए गए हैं। कथनों को सत्य मानते हुए, भले ही वे सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों से भिन्न प्रतीत हों, निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथनों से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>सभी Deal, Close हैं।<br>कुछ Close, Cross हैं।<br>कोई Deal, Drive नहीं है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ Close, Drive नहीं हैं।<br>II. सभी Cross, Close हैं।<br>III. कुछ Deal, Cross हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion III follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष III निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusions I and II follow","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I और II निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusions II and III follow","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II और III निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Every Deal is Close and no Deal is Drive, so the Deals are Close items that can never be Drive, and thus some Close items are not Drive<br>So conclusion I follows<br>Some Close is Cross does not make all Cross into Close, so II does not follow, and no link is given between Deal and Cross, so III does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक Deal, Close है और कोई Deal, Drive नहीं है, अतः Deal वे Close हैं जो कभी Drive नहीं हो सकते, और इसलिए कुछ Close, Drive नहीं हैं<br>अतः निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br>'कुछ Close, Cross हैं' से सभी Cross को Close नहीं कहा जा सकता, अतः II नहीं निकलता, तथा Deal और Cross के बीच कोई संबंध नहीं दिया गया, अतः III नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000074886","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, each letter is assigned a unique digit. Based on the given codes for specific words, determine the code for the target word using the same logic. If TRUST is coded as 73547 and HOPE as 2869, then how will THREE be coded? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में प्रत्येक अक्षर को एक अद्वितीय अंक दिया जाता है। विशिष्ट शब्दों के दिए गए कूटों के आधार पर उसी तर्क से लक्ष्य शब्द का कूट ज्ञात कीजिए। यदि TRUST का कूट 73547 है और HOPE का कूट 2869 है, तो THREE का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"72899"},"2":{"en":"73879"},"3":{"en":"74899"},"4":{"en":"72399"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In TRUST = 73547 the letter T comes at the first and the fourth place, and the digit 7 is also repeated at the first and the fourth place in the code, so T = 7<br>The pattern of the code follows the pattern of the letters: T R U S T → 7 3 5 4 7, so R = 3, U = 5 and S = 4<br>TRUST and HOPE together contain no repeated letters, so HOPE gives H = 2, O = 8, P = 6 and E = 9<br>Now THREE = T H R E E = 7 2 3 9 9<br>So THREE is coded as 72399<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 72399.</b>","hi":"TRUST = 73547 में अक्षर T पहले तथा चौथे स्थान पर है और कूट में अंक 7 भी पहले तथा चौथे स्थान पर दोहराया गया है, अतः T = 7<br>कूट का क्रम अक्षरों के क्रम के अनुसार है: T R U S T → 7 3 5 4 7, अतः R = 3, U = 5 तथा S = 4<br>TRUST और HOPE में मिलकर कोई अक्षर दोहराया नहीं गया, अतः HOPE से H = 2, O = 8, P = 6 तथा E = 9<br>अब THREE = T H R E E = 7 2 3 9 9<br>इसलिए THREE का कूट 72399 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 72399 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000074887","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '-' means '×', '+' means '÷', '×' means '+', then 15 − 3 + 6 × 2 = ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि '-' का अर्थ '×', '+' का अर्थ '÷' तथा '×' का अर्थ '+' है, तो 15 − 3 + 6 × 2 = ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"10"},"3":{"en":"8.5"},"4":{"en":"9.5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"After replacing the signs the expression becomes 15 × 3 ÷ 6 + 2<br>15 × 3 = 45 and 45 ÷ 6 = 7.5, then 7.5 + 2 = 9.5<br>So the value is 9.5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 9.5.</b>","hi":"चिह्न बदलने पर व्यंजक 15 × 3 ÷ 6 + 2 बनता है<br>15 × 3 = 45 तथा 45 ÷ 6 = 7.5, फिर 7.5 + 2 = 9.5<br>अतः मान 9.5 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 9.5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000074888","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code LETTER is coded as MFUUES, then how is MFUUES coded? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट में LETTER का कूट MFUUES है, तो MFUUES का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NGVVET"},"2":{"en":"NGWVFU"},"3":{"en":"NGVVFU"},"4":{"en":"NGVUET"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"LETTER → MFUUES: every letter moves one step ahead except the 5th letter, which stays the same (L→M, E→F, T→U, T→U, E, R→S)<br>MFUUES: M→N, F→G, U→V, U→V, E, S→T<br>Code = NGVVET<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): NGVVET.</b>","hi":"LETTER → MFUUES: पाँचवें अक्षर को छोड़कर प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ता है (L→M, E→F, T→U, T→U, E, R→S)<br>MFUUES: M→N, F→G, U→V, U→V, E, S→T<br>कूट = NGVVET<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): NGVVET है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000074889","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Carefully examine the address below and identify which of the following alternatives matches the given address.<br>Mrs. S. Iyer<br>3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj<br>New Delhi - 110070<br><b>Alternatives:</b><br>A) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 12th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110070<br>B) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110070<br>C) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110071<br>D) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110069 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"नीचे दिए पते को ध्यान से देखिए और पहचानिए कि निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है।<br>Mrs. S. Iyer<br>3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj<br>New Delhi - 110070<br><b>विकल्प:</b><br>A) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 12th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110070<br>B) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110070<br>C) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110071<br>D) Mrs. S. Iyer, 3048 Ashoka Residency, 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj, New Delhi - 110069 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only B","hi":"केवल B"},"2":{"en":"Only D","hi":"केवल D"},"3":{"en":"B and D","hi":"B और D"},"4":{"en":"D and C","hi":"D और C"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The given address has the house number 3048, the 11th Floor, Vasant Kunj and the pin code 110070<br>Alternative A changes the floor to the 12th, alternative C changes the pin code to 110071 and alternative D changes it to 110069<br>Only alternative B matches the given address in every part<br>Hence only B is the correct alternative<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only B.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में मकान संख्या 3048, 11वीं मंजिल, वसंत कुंज तथा पिन कोड 110070 है<br>विकल्प A में मंजिल 12वीं कर दी गई है, विकल्प C में पिन कोड 110071 तथा विकल्प D में 110069 कर दिया गया है<br>केवल विकल्प B हर भाग में दिए गए पते से मेल खाता है<br>अतः केवल B सही विकल्प है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल B है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000074890","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"DETERMINATION\" is written as \"DFTFRNIOAUIPN\". How will \"ORGANISATION\" be written? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"DETERMINATION\" को \"DFTFRNIOAUIPN\" लिखा जाता है। \"ORGANISATION\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"OSGBNJSBTOJO"},"2":{"en":"OSGBNJSBTJOO"},"3":{"en":"OSGBNSBJTJOO"},"4":{"en":"OSNBGJSJTJOO"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In DETERMINATION the letters at the odd places D, T, R, I, A, I, N stay where they are, and each letter at the even places moves one place ahead: E→F, E→F, M→N, N→O, T→U, O→P, which gives DFTFRNIOAUIPN<br>The same rule on ORGANISATION keeps O, G, N, S, T, O and moves R→S, A→B, I→J, A→B, I→J, N→O<br>So the code is OSGBNJSBTJOO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): OSGBNJSBTJOO.</b>","hi":"DETERMINATION में विषम स्थानों के अक्षर D, T, R, I, A, I, N अपने स्थान पर रहते हैं और सम स्थानों का प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ता है: E→F, E→F, M→N, N→O, T→U, O→P, जिससे DFTFRNIOAUIPN प्राप्त होता है<br>ORGANISATION पर वही नियम O, G, N, S, T, O को वैसा ही रखता है और R→S, A→B, I→J, A→B, I→J, N→O करता है<br>इसलिए कूट OSGBNJSBTJOO है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): OSGBNJSBTJOO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000074891","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.<br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है।<br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulvardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"},"2":{"en":"Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90071United States of America"},"3":{"en":"Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 17Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"},"4":{"en":"Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The original address has Unit 44A9, Tower 7, the word Boulevard and the code 90017<br>The first option writes Boulvard, the second option changes the code to 90071 and the third option changes the tower number to 17<br>Only the fourth option carries every part of the address exactly as given<br>Hence the fourth option perfectly matches the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America.</b>","hi":"मूल पते में Unit 44A9, Tower 7, शब्द Boulevard तथा कोड 90017 है<br>पहले विकल्प में Boulvard लिखा है, दूसरे विकल्प में कोड 90071 है तथा तीसरे विकल्प में tower संख्या 17 है<br>केवल चौथे विकल्प में पते का प्रत्येक भाग ठीक वैसा ही है<br>अतः चौथा विकल्प दिए गए पते से पूर्णतः मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Residence Unit 44A9Golden Palace Residency Tower 7Martin Luther King BoulevardLos Angeles California 90017United States of America है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000074892","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Suppose there is a family consisting of 6 individuals, P, Q, R, S, T, and U. The couple in the family are P and R. Q is the son of R. R is not the mother of Q. T is the sibling of R. S is the daughter of P. U is the brother of Q. How is U related to T? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान लीजिए एक परिवार में 6 व्यक्ति P, Q, R, S, T तथा U हैं। परिवार में युग्म P और R है। Q, R का पुत्र है। R, Q की माता नहीं है। T, R का सहोदर है। S, P की पुत्री है। U, Q का भाई है। U का T से क्या संबंध है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nephew","hi":"भतीजा"},"2":{"en":"Son","hi":"पुत्र"},"3":{"en":"Brother","hi":"भाई"},"4":{"en":"Paternal Uncle","hi":"चाचा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"63\" y=\"34\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"88\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M157 40H179M157 44H179M168 44V76M119 76H216M119 76V88M168 76V88M216 76V88M73 24H141M73 24V34M141 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"73\" y=\"48\">T</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"48\">P−</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"102\">Q+</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"102\">U+</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"102\">S−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>U is the son of R, and T is R's sibling, so U is T's nephew.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Nephew.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"63\" y=\"34\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"154\" y=\"88\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M157 40H179M157 44H179M168 44V76M119 76H216M119 76V88M168 76V88M216 76V88M73 24H141M73 24V34M141 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"73\" y=\"48\">T</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"48\">R+</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"48\">P−</text><text x=\"119\" y=\"102\">Q+</text><text x=\"168\" y=\"102\">U+</text><text x=\"216\" y=\"102\">S−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>U, R का पुत्र है तथा T, R का भाई/बहन है, अतः U, T का भतीजा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): भतीजा है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000074893","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Roll numbers follow the pattern: [First two digits] - [Difference between them] - [Last two digits]. Which is invalid roll number among the following options? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रोल नंबर इस पैटर्न का पालन करते हैं: [पहले दो अंक] - [उनके बीच का अंतर] - [अंतिम दो अंक]। निम्नलिखित विकल्पों में से कौन-सा रोल नंबर अमान्य है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"85-3-35"},"2":{"en":"92-7-25"},"3":{"en":"74-3-41"},"4":{"en":"61-6-16"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"For 85 the difference is 8 − 5 = 3 ✔, for 92 it is 9 − 2 = 7 ✔ and for 61 it is 6 − 1 = 5, which is printed as 6 ✘<br>For 74 the difference is 7 − 4 = 3 ✔<br>So 61-6-16 breaks the pattern and is the invalid roll number<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 61-6-16.</b>","hi":"85 के लिए अंतर 8 − 5 = 3 ✔, 92 के लिए 9 − 2 = 7 ✔ तथा 61 के लिए 6 − 1 = 5 है, जबकि मुद्रित अंतर 6 है ✘<br>74 के लिए 7 − 4 = 3 ✔<br>अतः 61-6-16 पैटर्न को तोड़ता है और अमान्य रोल नंबर है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 61-6-16 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000074894","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>MUS, QVW, UWA, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न जाँचिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>MUS, QVW, UWA, ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"YXE"},"2":{"en":"YYE"},"3":{"en":"YWE"},"4":{"en":"YXD"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters M, Q, U move four places ahead each time, so the next first letter is Y<br>The second letters U, V, W move one place ahead each time, so the next second letter is X<br>The third letters S, W, A move four places ahead each time, so after A the next third letter is E<br>Hence the next set of letters is YXE<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): YXE.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर M, Q, U प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर Y है<br>दूसरे अक्षर U, V, W प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर X है<br>तीसरे अक्षर S, W, A प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर E है<br>इसलिए अगला अक्षर-समूह YXE है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): YXE है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000074895","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"Analyse the given statement carefully, along with the proposed actions. Evaluate whether each of the actions is appropriate and sensible in the given context. Then select the option that correctly indicates which action(s) should be taken.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>One of the most important field operations by the company failed since the site manager underwent intense personal stress and could not coordinate adequately with the control room.<br><b>Course of Actions:</b><br>I. The organisation must conduct stress management screening and counseling to the managers who are in charge of critical assignments out in the field.<br>II. The site manager must be barred permanently from holding any position within the public sector. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिए गए कथन तथा प्रस्तावित कार्यवाहियों का ध्यानपूर्वक विश्लेषण कीजिए। मूल्यांकन कीजिए कि दी गई परिस्थिति में प्रत्येक कार्यवाही उपयुक्त तथा विवेकपूर्ण है या नहीं। फिर वह विकल्प चुनिए जो सही रूप से बताता है कि कौन-सी कार्यवाही की जानी चाहिए।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कंपनी का एक अत्यंत महत्वपूर्ण क्षेत्रीय अभियान विफल हो गया क्योंकि साइट मैनेजर गंभीर व्यक्तिगत तनाव में था और नियंत्रण कक्ष से ठीक से समन्वय नहीं कर सका।<br><b>कार्यवाहियाँ:</b><br>I. संगठन को क्षेत्र में महत्वपूर्ण कार्यों के प्रभारी प्रबंधकों के लिए तनाव प्रबंधन जाँच तथा परामर्श आयोजित करना चाहिए।<br>II. साइट मैनेजर को सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र में किसी भी पद पर स्थायी रूप से रोक लगा दिया जाना चाहिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows.","hi":"केवल I अनुसरण करता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows.","hi":"केवल II अनुसरण करता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow.","hi":"I और II दोनों अनुसरण करते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows.","hi":"न तो I और न ही II अनुसरण करता है।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The failure came from personal stress that spoiled coordination, so checking and counselling managers who handle critical field work attacks the real cause and prevents a repeat, which makes I appropriate<br>Barring the manager permanently from all public sector posts is far too harsh for a stress-related failure and is neither sensible nor proportionate, so II does not follow<br>Hence only course of action I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"विफलता व्यक्तिगत तनाव से हुई जिसने समन्वय बिगाड़ा, अतः महत्वपूर्ण क्षेत्रीय कार्य संभालने वाले प्रबंधकों की जाँच तथा परामर्श मूल कारण पर प्रहार करता है और पुनरावृत्ति रोकता है, इसलिए I उपयुक्त है<br>तनाव संबंधी विफलता के लिए प्रबंधक को सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के सभी पदों से स्थायी रूप से रोक देना अत्यधिक कठोर तथा असंगत है, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल कार्यवाही I निकलती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I अनुसरण करता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000074896","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">96</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। इस पैटर्न को पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">96</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">40</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"48"},"2":{"en":"72"},"3":{"en":"50"},"4":{"en":"64"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In every column the third number is the product of the sum and the difference of the first two numbers: (5 + 11) × (11 − 5) = 16 × 6 = 96 ✔ and (3 + 7) × (7 − 3) = 10 × 4 = 40 ✔<br>In the third column the same rule gives (6 + 10) × (10 − 6) = 16 × 4 = 64<br>So the missing number is 64<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 64.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक स्तंभ में तीसरी संख्या पहली दो संख्याओं के योग तथा अंतर का गुणनफल है: (5 + 11) × (11 − 5) = 16 × 6 = 96 ✔ तथा (3 + 7) × (7 − 3) = 10 × 4 = 40 ✔<br>तीसरे स्तंभ में वही नियम (6 + 10) × (10 − 6) = 16 × 4 = 64 देता है<br>अतः लुप्त संख्या 64 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 64 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000074897","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are leading a diverse task force that includes highly expressive extroverts and quiet, introverted analytical specialists. During brainstorming sessions, the expressive members dominate the conversation, while the quiet members say nothing, though their written reports are brilliant. How do you optimize this team's emotional and intellectual potential? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आप एक विविध कार्यदल का नेतृत्व कर रहे हैं जिसमें अत्यधिक अभिव्यक्तिशील बहिर्मुखी सदस्य तथा शांत, अंतर्मुखी विश्लेषणात्मक विशेषज्ञ हैं। विचार-मंथन सत्रों में अभिव्यक्तिशील सदस्य चर्चा पर हावी रहते हैं, जबकि शांत सदस्य कुछ नहीं कहते, यद्यपि उनकी लिखित रिपोर्ट उत्कृष्ट होती हैं। इस दल की भावनात्मक तथा बौद्धिक क्षमता का आप कैसे उपयोग करेंगे? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Assume that the quiet members simply have no verbal confidence and leave them out of future real-time strategy discussions.","hi":"यह मान लेना कि शांत सदस्यों में मौखिक आत्मविश्वास ही नहीं है और उन्हें भविष्य की तात्कालिक रणनीति चर्चाओं से बाहर रखना।"},"2":{"en":"Publicly call out the quiet members during meetings, demanding: \"Why are you sitting silently? Share an idea right now to prove your teamwork.\"","hi":"बैठक में शांत सदस्यों को सार्वजनिक रूप से ललकारते हुए कहना: \"आप चुप क्यों बैठे हैं? अपनी टीम भावना सिद्ध करने के लिए अभी विचार बताइए।\""},"3":{"en":"Revise the brainstorming: share the problem 24 hours early, collect anonymous digital inputs, and use the session to review ideas systematically.","hi":"विचार-मंथन का तरीका बदलना: समस्या 24 घंटे पहले साझा करना, गुमनाम डिजिटल सुझाव एकत्र करना और सत्र का उपयोग विचारों की क्रमबद्ध समीक्षा के लिए करना।"},"4":{"en":"Tell the expressive members to shut up for the first 30 minutes of the meeting so the quiet members are forced to fill the silence.","hi":"बैठक के पहले 30 मिनट अभिव्यक्तिशील सदस्यों को चुप रहने के लिए कहना ताकि शांत सदस्य मौन भरने के लिए बाध्य हों।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The quiet members are already producing excellent written work, so their ideas are valuable and the aim is to bring those ideas into the discussion without putting them on the spot<br>Sharing the problem in advance and collecting anonymous inputs lets them contribute in the calm manner that suits them, and the live session then becomes a systematic review of all ideas<br>Leaving them out loses their talent, calling them out publicly creates stress and silencing others only shifts the imbalance<br>So the third course of action optimizes the potential of everyone<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Revise the brainstorming: share the problem 24 hours early, collect anonymous digital inputs, and use the session to review ideas systematically.</b>","hi":"शांत सदस्य पहले ही उत्कृष्ट लिखित कार्य कर रहे हैं, अतः उनके विचार मूल्यवान हैं और उद्देश्य उन विचारों को दबाव डाले बिना चर्चा में लाना है<br>समस्या पहले से साझा करने तथा गुमनाम सुझाव लेने से वे अपने अनुकूल शांत ढंग से योगदान दे सकते हैं, और सत्र सभी विचारों की क्रमबद्ध समीक्षा बन जाता है<br>उन्हें बाहर रखने से प्रतिभा खो जाती है, सार्वजनिक ललकार तनाव पैदा करती है तथा दूसरों को चुप करा देना केवल असंतुलन बदल देता है<br>अतः तीसरी कार्यवाही सभी की क्षमता का सर्वोत्तम उपयोग करती है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): विचार-मंथन का तरीका बदलना: समस्या 24 घंटे पहले साझा करना, गुमनाम डिजिटल सुझाव एकत्र करना और सत्र का उपयोग विचारों की क्रमबद्ध समीक्षा के लिए करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000074898","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Choose the option which is exactly similar to: 18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प को चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है: 18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100 [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100"},"2":{"en":"18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-I, Bengaluru-560100"},"3":{"en":"18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-II, Bengaluru-560100"},"4":{"en":"18-05-2025, 1204, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The given address has the date 18-05-2026, the number 1024, Phase-III and the pin code 560100<br>The second option changes the phase to Phase-I, the third option to Phase-II, and the fourth option changes the year to 2025 and the number to 1204<br>Only the first option is exactly the same in every part<br>Hence the first option is exactly similar<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100.</b>","hi":"दिए गए पते में तिथि 18-05-2026, संख्या 1024, चरण Phase-III तथा पिन कोड 560100 है<br>दूसरे विकल्प में Phase-I, तीसरे विकल्प में Phase-II तथा चौथे विकल्प में वर्ष 2025 और संख्या 1204 है<br>केवल पहला विकल्प प्रत्येक भाग में ठीक वैसा ही है<br>अतः पहला विकल्प ठीक इसके समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 18-05-2026, 1024, High-Tech Industrial Estate, Phase-III, Bengaluru-560100 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000074899","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>A1Z : B4Y :: C9X : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>A1Z : B4Y :: C9X : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"D16W"},"2":{"en":"D15W"},"3":{"en":"E16W"},"4":{"en":"D16V"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letter moves one place ahead: A → B → C → D, the middle number is the square of the position of the first letter: 1² = 1, 2² = 4, 3² = 9, 4² = 16, and the last letter moves one place back: Z → Y → X → W<br>Applying this to C9X gives D16W<br>Hence the answer is D16W<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): D16W.</b>","hi":"पहला अक्षर एक स्थान आगे बढ़ता है: A → B → C → D, बीच की संख्या पहले अक्षर के स्थान का वर्ग है: 1² = 1, 2² = 4, 3² = 9, 4² = 16, तथा अंतिम अक्षर एक स्थान पीछे जाता है: Z → Y → X → W<br>C9X पर यही लागू करने से D16W प्राप्त होता है<br>अतः उत्तर D16W है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): D16W है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000074900","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 20 &#9673; 5 &#8853; 3 = 1 and 45 &#9673; 9 &#8853; 2 = 3, then what will be the value of 60 &#9673; 6 &#8853; 7? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 20 &#9673; 5 &#8853; 3 = 1 तथा 45 &#9673; 9 &#8853; 2 = 3 है, तो 60 &#9673; 6 &#8853; 7 का मान क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"7"},"4":{"en":"9"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the first equation 20 &#9673; 5 gives 4 and 4 &#8853; 3 gives 1, so &#9673; means division and &#8853; means subtraction<br>Checking the second equation, 45 &#9673; 9 = 5 and 5 &#8853; 2 = 3 ✔<br>So 60 &#9673; 6 = 10 and 10 &#8853; 7 = 3<br>Hence the value is 3<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 3.</b>","hi":"पहले समीकरण में 20 &#9673; 5 = 4 तथा 4 &#8853; 3 = 1 है, अतः &#9673; का अर्थ भाग तथा &#8853; का अर्थ घटाना है<br>दूसरा समीकरण जाँचने पर 45 &#9673; 9 = 5 तथा 5 &#8853; 2 = 3 ✔<br>अतः 60 &#9673; 6 = 10 तथा 10 &#8853; 7 = 3<br>इसलिए मान 3 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000074901","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the eligibility criteria given for the post carefully and answer the question that follows.<br><b>Eligibility Criteria for Assistant Section Officer (ASO):</b><br>1. Age: 18–27 years.<br>2. Physical standard: Height of at least 165 cm.<br>3. Must hold a valid driving license.<br><b>Case:</b> Rohan is 25 years old, 168 cm tall, and does not possess a driving license.<br>What should be done in Rohan's case? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पद के लिए दी गई पात्रता शर्तें ध्यान से पढ़िए और आगे दिए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br><b>सहायक अनुभाग अधिकारी (ASO) के लिए पात्रता शर्तें:</b><br>1. आयु: 18–27 वर्ष।<br>2. शारीरिक मानक: कम से कम 165 सेमी की लंबाई।<br>3. वैध ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस होना आवश्यक है।<br><b>मामला:</b> रोहन 25 वर्ष का है, 168 सेमी लंबा है और उसके पास ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस नहीं है।<br>रोहन के मामले में क्या किया जाना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Eligible","hi":"पात्र"},"2":{"en":"Not Eligible (Age more)","hi":"अपात्र (आयु अधिक)"},"3":{"en":"Not Eligible (Height less)","hi":"अपात्र (लंबाई कम)"},"4":{"en":"Not Eligible (No driving license)","hi":"अपात्र (ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस नहीं)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Rohan is 25 years old, which is within the age limit of 18 to 27 years, so the age condition is satisfied<br>His height is 168 cm, which is more than the required 165 cm, so the height condition is also satisfied<br>He does not hold a driving license, which is the third requirement, so this condition fails<br>Hence Rohan is not eligible because he has no driving license<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Not Eligible (No driving license).</b>","hi":"रोहन 25 वर्ष का है, जो 18 से 27 वर्ष की आयु सीमा में है, अतः आयु की शर्त पूरी होती है<br>उसकी लंबाई 168 सेमी है, जो आवश्यक 165 सेमी से अधिक है, अतः लंबाई की शर्त भी पूरी होती है<br>उसके पास ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस नहीं है, जो तीसरी आवश्यकता है, अतः यह शर्त पूरी नहीं होती<br>इसलिए रोहन ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस न होने के कारण अपात्र है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): अपात्र (ड्राइविंग लाइसेंस नहीं) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000074902","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Data Center Administrator Selection:</b><br>(i) Degree in Computer Science.<br>(ii) 4+ years of network experience.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception 1:</b> If a candidate has a Degree in Computer Science and exactly 3 years of network experience, provided they hold a professional certification, the case must be referred to the Department Head.<br><b>Exception 2:</b> If a candidate has a Degree in Computer Science and 5+ years of network experience, they are eligible for a direct promotion to Senior Administrator.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate holds a degree in Computer Science, has 3 years of network experience, and possesses a relevant professional certification. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई शर्तें ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू होता है, तो वह प्राधिकारी पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>डेटा सेंटर प्रशासक चयन के लिए मानदंड:</b><br>(i) कंप्यूटर विज्ञान में डिग्री।<br>(ii) 4+ वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद 1:</b> यदि किसी अभ्यर्थी के पास कंप्यूटर विज्ञान में डिग्री और ठीक 3 वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव है, बशर्ते उसके पास पेशेवर प्रमाणन हो, तो मामला विभागाध्यक्ष को भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद 2:</b> यदि किसी अभ्यर्थी के पास कंप्यूटर विज्ञान में डिग्री और 5+ वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव है, तो वह वरिष्ठ प्रशासक के पद पर सीधी पदोन्नति के लिए पात्र है।<br><b>मामला:</b> अभ्यर्थी के पास कंप्यूटर विज्ञान में डिग्री है, 3 वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव है और प्रासंगिक पेशेवर प्रमाणन है। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Candidate is selected.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी चयनित किया जाता है।"},"2":{"en":"Candidate is rejected as they do not meet the primary criteria of 4+ years of network experience.","hi":"अभ्यर्थी को अस्वीकार किया जाता है क्योंकि वह 4+ वर्ष के नेटवर्क अनुभव की प्राथमिक शर्त पूरी नहीं करता।"},"3":{"en":"Refer the case to the Department Head.","hi":"मामला विभागाध्यक्ष को भेजा जाए।"},"4":{"en":"Candidate is eligible for direct promotion to Senior Administrator based on their experience and professional certification.","hi":"अनुभव और पेशेवर प्रमाणन के आधार पर अभ्यर्थी वरिष्ठ प्रशासक पर सीधी पदोन्नति के लिए पात्र है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The main criteria need 4 or more years of network experience, and the candidate has only 3 years, so the case does not fit the main rule<br>Exception 1 covers exactly a candidate with a Computer Science degree, exactly 3 years of network experience and a professional certification, and all three are present here<br>So the case must be referred to the Department Head, while Exception 2 needs 5 or more years and does not apply<br>Hence the case is referred to the Department Head<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Refer the case to the Department Head.</b>","hi":"मुख्य मानदंड के लिए 4 या अधिक वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव चाहिए और अभ्यर्थी के पास केवल 3 वर्ष हैं, अतः मामला मुख्य नियम में नहीं बैठता<br>अपवाद 1 ठीक उसी अभ्यर्थी के लिए है जिसके पास कंप्यूटर विज्ञान की डिग्री, ठीक 3 वर्ष का नेटवर्क अनुभव तथा पेशेवर प्रमाणन हो, और यहाँ तीनों उपस्थित हैं<br>अतः मामला विभागाध्यक्ष को भेजा जाना चाहिए, जबकि अपवाद 2 के लिए 5 या अधिक वर्ष चाहिए और वह लागू नहीं होता<br>इसलिए मामला विभागाध्यक्ष को भेजा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): मामला विभागाध्यक्ष को भेजा जाए। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000074903","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>A wildlife reserve has restricted vehicle access to certain sensitive zones during the breeding season of endangered species.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Endangered species can survive only in areas where vehicle access is completely prohibited.<br>II. The reserve authorities believe human activity may affect the breeding process of endangered species. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>एक वन्यजीव अभयारण्य ने लुप्तप्राय प्रजातियों के प्रजनन काल के दौरान कुछ संवेदनशील क्षेत्रों में वाहनों के प्रवेश को सीमित कर दिया है।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. लुप्तप्राय प्रजातियाँ केवल उन्हीं क्षेत्रों में जीवित रह सकती हैं जहाँ वाहनों का प्रवेश पूर्णतः प्रतिबंधित हो।<br>II. अभयारण्य प्राधिकरण का मानना है कि मानवीय गतिविधि लुप्तप्राय प्रजातियों की प्रजनन प्रक्रिया को प्रभावित कर सकती है। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Restricting vehicles in the breeding season shows that the authorities expect disturbance from vehicles, that is human activity, to harm breeding, so conclusion II follows<br>The restriction is only for certain zones and only for a season, so it does not say that the species survive only where vehicles are fully banned, and conclusion I does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion II follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion II follows.</b>","hi":"प्रजनन काल में वाहनों को सीमित करना दर्शाता है कि प्राधिकरण मानते हैं कि वाहनों से होने वाला व्यवधान अर्थात् मानवीय गतिविधि प्रजनन को हानि पहुँचा सकती है, अतः निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br>प्रतिबंध केवल कुछ क्षेत्रों तथा केवल एक मौसम के लिए है, अतः यह नहीं कहा गया कि प्रजातियाँ केवल वहीं जीवित रह सकती हैं जहाँ वाहन पूर्णतः प्रतिबंधित हैं, अतः निष्कर्ष I नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000074904","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Urban planners should prioritize the construction of dedicated bicycle lanes in all new city infrastructure projects to promote healthier transportation alternatives.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. The current infrastructure is not adequately equipped to ensure the safety of urban cyclists.<br>II. A significant number of citizens are willing to commute by bicycle if the facilities exist. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित निम्नलिखित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>शहरी आयोजकों को स्वस्थ परिवहन विकल्पों को बढ़ावा देने के लिए सभी नई शहरी अवसंरचना परियोजनाओं में समर्पित साइकिल लेन के निर्माण को प्राथमिकता देनी चाहिए।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. वर्तमान अवसंरचना शहरी साइकिल चालकों की सुरक्षा सुनिश्चित करने के लिए पर्याप्त रूप से सुसज्जित नहीं है।<br>II. यदि सुविधाएँ उपलब्ध हों तो पर्याप्त संख्या में नागरिक साइकिल से आवागमन के लिए तैयार हैं। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"3":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Building dedicated bicycle lanes makes sense only if cyclists are today unsafe on the existing roads, so the first assumption is implicit<br>The lanes are also meant to promote healthier transport, which is possible only if enough citizens are ready to cycle once the facilities exist, so the second assumption is also implicit<br>Hence both assumptions are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Both Assumptions I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"समर्पित साइकिल लेन बनाना तभी तर्कसंगत है जब आज मौजूदा सड़कों पर साइकिल चालक सुरक्षित न हों, अतः पहली अवधारणा निहित है<br>ये लेन स्वस्थ परिवहन को बढ़ावा देने के लिए हैं, जो तभी संभव है जब सुविधाएँ मिलने पर पर्याप्त नागरिक साइकिल चलाने को तैयार हों, अतः दूसरी अवधारणा भी निहित है<br>इसलिए दोनों अवधारणाएँ निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000074905","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Leveret : Hare :: Gosling : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस विकल्प का चयन कीजिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्दों को अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द मानना है और उनके अक्षरों की संख्या/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर परस्पर संबंध नहीं मानना है।)<br>Leveret : Hare :: Gosling : ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Duck"},"2":{"en":"Swan"},"3":{"en":"Hen"},"4":{"en":"Goose"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A leveret is the young one of a hare, so the pair shows an animal's young and the animal<br>The young one of a goose is called a gosling, so the third word is related to Goose in the same way<br>Duck, swan and hen have their own different names for their young, so they do not fit<br>Hence the answer is Goose<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Goose.</b>","hi":"Leveret, खरगोश (Hare) का शिशु है, अतः युग्म पशु के शिशु और पशु का संबंध दर्शाता है<br>हंस (Goose) के शिशु को Gosling कहा जाता है, अतः तीसरा शब्द उसी प्रकार Goose से संबंधित है<br>बत्तख, राजहंस तथा मुर्गी के शिशुओं के अपने अलग नाम हैं, अतः वे इस संबंध में नहीं बैठते<br>इसलिए उत्तर Goose है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Goose है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000074906","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a significant environmental concern in the Indian Ocean? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी हिंद महासागर की एक महत्वपूर्ण पर्यावरणीय चिंता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Melting polar ice caps","hi":"ध्रुवीय हिम टोपियों का पिघलना"},"2":{"en":"Desertification","hi":"मरुस्थलीकरण"},"3":{"en":"Coral reef bleaching","hi":"प्रवाल भित्ति विरंजन"},"4":{"en":"Deforestation","hi":"वनोन्मूलन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Coral reef bleaching</b><br><b>Coral reef bleaching</b> is a significant environmental concern in the <b>Indian Ocean</b>, where rising sea temperatures due to climate change have caused repeated mass bleaching events in the Andaman, Lakshadweep, Maldives and Gulf of Mannar reefs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bleaching occurs when heat stress makes corals expel their symbiotic <b>zooxanthellae</b>, losing colour and their main food source.<br>• The Indian Ocean has warmed faster than most oceans, and the <b>2016 El Niño</b> caused severe bleaching in the Andaman and Nicobar reefs.<br>• Other concerns for the Indian Ocean include <b>ocean acidification, plastic pollution, overfishing and sea-level rise</b>.<br>• Melting polar ice caps and deforestation are global or terrestrial issues, and desertification is mainly a land-based problem, so they are not specific to the Indian Ocean.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because coral reef bleaching is a major Indian Ocean concern.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – प्रवाल भित्ति विरंजन</b><br><b>प्रवाल भित्ति विरंजन (Coral reef bleaching)</b> <b>हिंद महासागर</b> की एक महत्वपूर्ण पर्यावरणीय चिंता है, जहाँ जलवायु परिवर्तन से बढ़ते समुद्री तापमान ने अंडमान, लक्षद्वीप, मालदीव तथा मन्नार की खाड़ी की भित्तियों में बार-बार सामूहिक विरंजन किया है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विरंजन तब होता है जब ऊष्मा तनाव से प्रवाल अपने सहजीवी <b>ज़ूजैंथेली</b> को बाहर निकाल देते हैं, जिससे रंग तथा मुख्य आहार-स्रोत दोनों जाते हैं।<br>• हिंद महासागर अधिकांश महासागरों की तुलना में अधिक तेजी से गर्म हुआ है, और <b>2016 के एल-नीनो</b> से अंडमान एवं निकोबार की भित्तियों में गंभीर विरंजन हुआ।<br>• हिंद महासागर की अन्य चिंताएँ <b>महासागरीय अम्लीकरण, प्लास्टिक प्रदूषण, अत्यधिक मत्स्यन तथा समुद्री जलस्तर वृद्धि</b> हैं।<br>• ध्रुवीय हिम टोपियों का पिघलना तथा वनोन्मूलन वैश्विक या स्थलीय विषय हैं, और मरुस्थलीकरण मुख्यतः भूमि-आधारित समस्या है, इसलिए ये हिंद महासागर-विशिष्ट नहीं हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्रवाल भित्ति विरंजन हिंद महासागर की प्रमुख चिंता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000074907","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"Which of the following is NOT a focus area for QUAD (Quadrilateral Security Dialogue)? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा क्वाड (चतुर्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद) का केंद्रित क्षेत्र नहीं है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Maritime security","hi":"समुद्री सुरक्षा"},"2":{"en":"Space cooperation","hi":"अंतरिक्ष सहयोग"},"3":{"en":"Cybersecurity","hi":"साइबर सुरक्षा"},"4":{"en":"Nuclear disarmament","hi":"परमाणु निरस्त्रीकरण"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Nuclear disarmament</b><br><b>Nuclear disarmament</b> is not a focus area of the <b>Quad (Quadrilateral Security Dialogue)</b>, whose agenda centres on a free and open Indo-Pacific, maritime security, cyber security, space cooperation and critical technologies.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Quad comprises <b>India, the United States, Japan and Australia</b> and works through working groups on vaccines, critical and emerging technologies, climate and connectivity.<br>• Its initiatives include the <b>Quad Maritime Domain Awareness Partnership, the Indo-Pacific Partnership for Maritime Domain Awareness (IPMDA) and the Quad Satellite Data Portal</b>.<br>• The group is a consultative, non-treaty forum and has no mutual defence commitment; two of its members, India and Japan, are not nuclear-weapon states under the NPT.<br>• Nuclear disarmament is discussed in the United Nations and the NPT review process, not in the Quad.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because nuclear disarmament is not a Quad focus area.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – परमाणु निरस्त्रीकरण</b><br><b>परमाणु निरस्त्रीकरण</b> <b>क्वाड (चतुर्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद)</b> का केंद्रित क्षेत्र नहीं है, जिसकी कार्यसूची स्वतंत्र एवं खुले इंडो-पैसिफिक, समुद्री सुरक्षा, साइबर सुरक्षा, अंतरिक्ष सहयोग तथा महत्वपूर्ण प्रौद्योगिकियों पर केंद्रित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• क्वाड में <b>भारत, संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका, जापान तथा ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> सम्मिलित हैं और यह टीके, महत्वपूर्ण एवं उभरती प्रौद्योगिकियों, जलवायु तथा संपर्क पर कार्यसमूहों के माध्यम से कार्य करता है।<br>• इसकी पहलों में <b>क्वाड समुद्री क्षेत्र जागरूकता साझेदारी, इंडो-पैसिफिक मैरीटाइम डोमेन अवेयरनेस पार्टनरशिप (IPMDA) तथा क्वाड उपग्रह डेटा पोर्टल</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• यह समूह परामर्शात्मक, संधि-रहित मंच है और इसकी कोई पारस्परिक रक्षा प्रतिबद्धता नहीं है; इसके दो सदस्य भारत तथा जापान NPT के अंतर्गत परमाणु-हथियार संपन्न राज्य नहीं हैं।<br>• परमाणु निरस्त्रीकरण पर संयुक्त राष्ट्र तथा NPT समीक्षा प्रक्रिया में विचार होता है, क्वाड में नहीं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि परमाणु निरस्त्रीकरण क्वाड का केंद्रित क्षेत्र नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000074908","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"What is the term for a 'draw' in a chess match? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"शतरंज के खेल में 'ड्रॉ' (बराबरी) के लिए किस शब्द का प्रयोग होता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Checkmate","hi":"चेकमेट"},"2":{"en":"Stalemate","hi":"स्टेलमेट"},"3":{"en":"Gambit","hi":"गैंबिट"},"4":{"en":"Castling","hi":"कैसलिंग"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Stalemate</b><br><b>Stalemate</b> is a position in chess in which the player whose turn it is <b>has no legal move</b> but is <b>not in check</b>, and the game is declared a <b>draw</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Checkmate</b> is a win, when the king is in check and there is no legal move to escape.<br>• A <b>gambit</b> is an opening in which material is sacrificed for a positional advantage, and <b>castling</b> is a special joint move of the king and rook.<br>• Other ways of drawing a game include <b>agreement, threefold repetition, the fifty-move rule and insufficient material</b>.<br>• Each player starts with <b>16 pieces</b>, and white moves first; the world body is FIDE.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because stalemate results in a draw in chess.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – स्टेलमेट</b><br><b>स्टेलमेट (Stalemate)</b> शतरंज की वह स्थिति है जिसमें जिस खिलाड़ी की चाल है उसके पास <b>कोई वैध चाल नहीं</b> होती, परंतु उसका राजा <b>शह नहीं</b> होता, और खेल <b>बराबर (draw)</b> घोषित हो जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>चेकमेट</b> जीत होती है, जब राजा शह में हो और बचने की कोई वैध चाल न हो।<br>• <b>गैंबिट</b> वह शुरुआती चालक्रम है जिसमें स्थितिगत लाभ के लिए मोहरा त्यागा जाता है, और <b>कैसलिंग</b> राजा तथा हाथी की विशेष संयुक्त चाल है।<br>• बराबरी के अन्य तरीके हैं – <b>सहमति, तीन बार पुनरावृत्ति, पचास चाल का नियम तथा अपर्याप्त सामग्री</b>।<br>• प्रत्येक खिलाड़ी के पास आरंभ में <b>16 मोहरे</b> होते हैं और श्वेत पहले चलता है; विश्व निकाय FIDE है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि शतरंज में स्टेलमेट से बराबरी होती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000074909","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which author wrote “The Golden House” and “Quichotte,” both longlisted for the Booker Prize, but neither won it? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस लेखक ने \"द गोल्डन हाउस\" तथा \"क्विशोट\" लिखा, जो दोनों बुकर पुरस्कार की लंबी सूची में थे, परंतु कोई भी पुरस्कार नहीं जीता? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Arundhati Roy","hi":"अरुंधति रॉय"},"2":{"en":"Amitav Ghosh","hi":"अमिताव घोष"},"3":{"en":"Salman Rushdie","hi":"सलमान रुश्दी"},"4":{"en":"Kiran Nagarkar","hi":"किरण नगरकर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Salman Rushdie</b><br><b>Salman Rushdie</b> wrote <b>'The Golden House' (2017)</b> and <b>'Quichotte' (2019)</b>, both of which were longlisted for the <b>Booker Prize</b> but did not win it.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Rushdie won the <b>Booker Prize in 1981</b> for <b>'Midnight's Children'</b>, which was also voted the 'Booker of Bookers'.<br>• 'Quichotte' was shortlisted for the Booker Prize in 2019, while 'The Golden House' made the longlist in 2017.<br>• <b>Arundhati Roy</b> won the Booker in 1997 for 'The God of Small Things', and <b>Amitav Ghosh</b> was shortlisted for 'Sea of Poppies' in 2008.<br>• Rushdie received the <b>Booker Prize's special awards</b> and was knighted in 2007; his memoir is 'Knife'.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Salman Rushdie wrote both 'The Golden House' and 'Quichotte'.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सलमान रुश्दी</b><br><b>सलमान रुश्दी (Salman Rushdie)</b> ने <b>'द गोल्डन हाउस' (2017)</b> तथा <b>'क्विशोट' (2019)</b> लिखीं, जिनमें से दोनों <b>बुकर पुरस्कार</b> की लंबी सूची में थीं, परंतु कोई पुरस्कार नहीं जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• रुश्दी ने <b>1981 में 'मिडनाइट्स चिल्ड्रन'</b> के लिए <b>बुकर पुरस्कार</b> जीता था, जिसे 'बुकर ऑफ बुकर्स' भी चुना गया।<br>• 'क्विशोट' 2019 में बुकर पुरस्कार की लघु सूची में थी, जबकि 'द गोल्डन हाउस' 2017 में लंबी सूची में आई।<br>• <b>अरुंधति रॉय</b> ने 1997 में 'द गॉड ऑफ स्मॉल थिंग्स' के लिए बुकर जीता, और <b>अमिताव घोष</b> 'सी ऑफ पॉपीज़' के लिए 2008 में लघु सूची में थे।<br>• रुश्दी को <b>बुकर पुरस्कार के विशेष सम्मान</b> मिले और 2007 में उन्हें नाइटहुड प्रदान किया गया; उनकी संस्मरण पुस्तक 'नाइफ' है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 'द गोल्डन हाउस' तथा 'क्विशोट' दोनों सलमान रुश्दी ने लिखीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000074910","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"The significant devaluation of the Indian rupee in 1966 (from ₹4.76 to ₹7.50 per USD) was largely a result of the economic challenges and policy failures associated with the ______ Five-Year Plan. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1966 में भारतीय रुपये का उल्लेखनीय अवमूल्यन (₹4.76 से ₹7.50 प्रति USD) काफी हद तक ______ पंचवर्षीय योजना से जुड़ी आर्थिक चुनौतियों तथा नीतिगत विफलताओं का परिणाम था। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"First","hi":"प्रथम"},"2":{"en":"Second","hi":"द्वितीय"},"3":{"en":"Third","hi":"तृतीय"},"4":{"en":"Fourth","hi":"चतुर्थ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Third</b><br>The <b>devaluation of the rupee in June 1966</b> from ₹4.76 to ₹7.50 per US dollar followed the economic difficulties of the <b>Third Five-Year Plan (1961-66)</b>, which was marked by war, drought and a foreign exchange crisis.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Third Plan's failures were compounded by the <b>1962 China war, the 1965 Pakistan war and drought</b>, leading to a food and forex crisis and dependence on PL-480 imports.<br>• The <b>First Plan (1951-56)</b> focused on agriculture, the <b>Second (1956-61)</b> on heavy industry under the Mahalanobis model, and the <b>Fourth (1969-74)</b> on growth with stability and self-reliance.<br>• The rupee was devalued again in <b>1991</b> in two installments during the balance of payments crisis.<br>• The Third Plan also saw the creation of the <b>National Food Security policy and the Green Revolution</b> programme later in the decade.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the 1966 devaluation is linked with the Third Plan's economic challenges.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – तृतीय</b><br><b>जून 1966 में रुपये का अवमूल्यन</b> ₹4.76 से ₹7.50 प्रति अमेरिकी डॉलर होने के पीछे <b>तृतीय पंचवर्षीय योजना (1961-66)</b> की आर्थिक कठिनाइयाँ थीं, जो युद्ध, सूखा तथा विदेशी मुद्रा संकट से चिह्नित रही।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• तृतीय योजना की विफलताएँ <b>1962 के चीन युद्ध, 1965 के पाकिस्तान युद्ध तथा सूखे</b> से और बढ़ीं, जिससे खाद्य एवं विदेशी मुद्रा संकट तथा PL-480 आयातों पर निर्भरता आई।<br>• <b>प्रथम योजना (1951-56)</b> कृषि पर, <b>द्वितीय (1956-61)</b> महालनोबिस मॉडल के अंतर्गत भारी उद्योग पर तथा <b>चतुर्थ (1969-74)</b> स्थिरता के साथ वृद्धि एवं आत्मनिर्भरता पर केंद्रित रही।<br>• भुगतान संतुलन संकट के दौरान <b>1991</b> में रुपये का अवमूल्यन दो चरणों में पुनः हुआ।<br>• तृतीय योजना के काल में ही बाद में <b>राष्ट्रीय खाद्य सुरक्षा नीति तथा हरित क्रांति</b> कार्यक्रम आरंभ हुए।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि 1966 का अवमूल्यन तृतीय योजना की आर्थिक चुनौतियों से जुड़ा है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000074911","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a national kabaddi championship in India? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी भारत में एक राष्ट्रीय कबड्डी चैंपियनशिप है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PKL","hi":"प्रो कबड्डी लीग (PKL)"},"2":{"en":"Kabaddi League","hi":"कबड्डी लीग"},"3":{"en":"Federation Cup","hi":"फेडरेशन कप"},"4":{"en":"Senior Nationals","hi":"सीनियर नेशनल्स"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Senior Nationals</b><br>The <b>Senior National Kabaddi Championship</b> is the national championship of India, organised by the <b>Amateur Kabaddi Federation of India</b>, in which state teams compete for the national title.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The <b>Pro Kabaddi League (PKL)</b> is a franchise-based professional league launched in 2014, not a national championship.<br>• The AKFI also conducts the <b>Junior Nationals, Federation Cup and inter-zonal championships</b>; the Federation Cup is a tournament, not the national championship.<br>• Kabaddi is the <b>national game of Bangladesh</b> and a traditional Indian sport, included in the Asian Games since 1990.<br>• India has won the <b>Asian Games kabaddi gold</b> in the men's event on most occasions and won the Kabaddi World Cup in 2004, 2007 and 2016.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the Senior Nationals is India's national kabaddi championship.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – सीनियर नेशनल्स</b><br><b>सीनियर राष्ट्रीय कबड्डी चैंपियनशिप</b> भारत की राष्ट्रीय चैंपियनशिप है, जिसे <b>अमेच्योर कबड्डी फेडरेशन ऑफ इंडिया</b> आयोजित करता है और जिसमें राज्यों की टीमें राष्ट्रीय खिताब के लिए खेलती हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>प्रो कबड्डी लीग (PKL)</b> 2014 में शुरू फ्रैंचाइज़ी-आधारित व्यावसायिक लीग है, राष्ट्रीय चैंपियनशिप नहीं।<br>• AKFI <b>जूनियर नेशनल्स, फेडरेशन कप तथा अंतर-क्षेत्रीय चैंपियनशिप</b> भी आयोजित करता है; फेडरेशन कप एक टूर्नामेंट है, राष्ट्रीय चैंपियनशिप नहीं।<br>• कबड्डी <b>बांग्लादेश का राष्ट्रीय खेल</b> है और एक परंपरागत भारतीय खेल है, जो 1990 से एशियाई खेलों में सम्मिलित है।<br>• भारत ने <b>एशियाई खेलों की कबड्डी में पुरुष वर्ग का स्वर्ण</b> अधिकांश बार जीता है तथा 2004, 2007 और 2016 में कबड्डी विश्व कप जीता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि सीनियर नेशनल्स भारत की राष्ट्रीय कबड्डी चैंपियनशिप है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000074912","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"Which of the following festivals marks the beginning of the New Year in the traditional Sikh calendar? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा उत्सव पारंपरिक सिख पंचांग में नववर्ष के आरंभ का प्रतीक है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Guru Nanak Jayanti","hi":"गुरु नानक जयंती"},"2":{"en":"Vaisakhi","hi":"वैसाखी"},"3":{"en":"Lohri","hi":"लोहड़ी"},"4":{"en":"Bandi Chhor Divas","hi":"बंदी छोड़ दिवस"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Vaisakhi</b><br><b>Vaisakhi</b>, celebrated on <b>13 or 14 April</b>, marks the beginning of the new year in the traditional Sikh (Nanakshahi) calendar and also commemorates the founding of the <b>Khalsa Panth by Guru Gobind Singh in 1699</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Vaisakhi is the harvest festival of Punjab and is celebrated with <b>Bhangra and Gidda</b> dances and processions (Nagar Kirtan).<br>• <b>Guru Nanak Jayanti</b> marks the birth of Guru Nanak (Kartik Purnima), <b>Lohri</b> is a winter harvest festival in January and <b>Bandi Chhor Divas</b> marks Guru Hargobind's release from Gwalior fort, celebrated with Diwali.<br>• The <b>Nanakshahi calendar</b>, adopted in 2003, fixes Sikh festival dates and begins with the month of Chet.<br>• Vaisakhi is also the new year in several other Indian calendars such as Bihu (Assam) and Puthandu (Tamil Nadu).<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Vaisakhi marks the Sikh new year.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वैसाखी</b><br><b>वैसाखी</b>, जो <b>13 या 14 अप्रैल</b> को मनाई जाती है, पारंपरिक सिख (नानकशाही) पंचांग में नववर्ष का आरंभ करती है और <b>1699 में गुरु गोबिंद सिंह द्वारा खालसा पंथ की स्थापना</b> की भी स्मृति है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• वैसाखी पंजाब का फसल उत्सव है, जिसे <b>भांगड़ा तथा गिद्दा</b> नृत्य और नगर कीर्तन के साथ मनाया जाता है।<br>• <b>गुरु नानक जयंती</b> गुरु नानक के जन्म (कार्तिक पूर्णिमा) की, <b>लोहड़ी</b> जनवरी का शीतकालीन फसल उत्सव है, तथा <b>बंदी छोड़ दिवस</b> गुरु हरगोबिंद की ग्वालियर किले से मुक्ति की स्मृति है, जो दिवाली के साथ मनाया जाता है।<br>• 2003 में अपनाया गया <b>नानकशाही पंचांग</b> सिख उत्सवों की तिथियाँ निर्धारित करता है और चेत मास से आरंभ होता है।<br>• वैसाखी बिहू (असम) तथा पुथांडु (तमिलनाडु) जैसे कई अन्य भारतीय पंचांगों में भी नववर्ष है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि वैसाखी सिख नववर्ष का प्रतीक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000074913","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"Which of the following key changes is introduced in the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023, replacing the Indian Penal Code (IPC) of 1860? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय दंड संहिता (IPC), 1860 के स्थान पर भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा प्रमुख परिवर्तन लाया गया है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Introduction of Community Service as a form of punishment","hi":"दंड के रूप में सामुदायिक सेवा का प्रावधान"},"2":{"en":"Replacement of all criminal laws with a common civil code","hi":"सभी आपराधिक विधियों का सामान्य नागरिक संहिता से प्रतिस्थापन"},"3":{"en":"Removal of Sedition Law without any replacement","hi":"बिना किसी प्रतिस्थापन के राजद्रोह विधि का हटाया जाना"},"4":{"en":"Complete abolition of capital punishment","hi":"मृत्युदंड का पूर्ण उन्मूलन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Introduction of Community Service as a form of punishment</b><br>The <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> introduced <b>community service</b> as a form of punishment for the first time, for offences such as defamation, public servant misconduct, attempt to suicide to compel a public servant and small theft.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Community service is listed in <b>Section 4</b> of the BNS along with death, imprisonment and fine as a recognised punishment.<br>• The BNS does <b>not</b> abolish capital punishment; death penalty remains for offences such as murder and rape of a child.<br>• Sedition was <b>not simply removed</b>; Section 124A of the IPC was replaced by a new offence of acts endangering the sovereignty, unity and integrity of India.<br>• The BNS is a criminal code and does not replace all criminal laws with a civil code; the BNSS and BSA deal with procedure and evidence.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because community service as a punishment is a key change in the BNS.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – दंड के रूप में सामुदायिक सेवा का प्रावधान</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023</b> में पहली बार <b>सामुदायिक सेवा</b> को दंड के रूप में जोड़ा गया है, जैसे मानहानि, लोक सेवक के कदाचार, लोक सेवक को विवश करने हेतु आत्महत्या का प्रयास तथा छोटी चोरी जैसे अपराधों के लिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सामुदायिक सेवा को BNS की <b>धारा 4</b> में मृत्यु, कारावास तथा जुर्माने के साथ मान्य दंड के रूप में सूचीबद्ध किया गया है।<br>• BNS <b>मृत्युदंड समाप्त नहीं करती</b>; हत्या तथा बालिका के बलात्कार जैसे अपराधों के लिए मृत्युदंड बना रहता है।<br>• राजद्रोह को <b>केवल हटाया नहीं गया</b>; IPC की धारा 124A के स्थान पर संप्रभुता, एकता तथा अखंडता को संकट में डालने वाले कृत्य का नया अपराध आया।<br>• BNS आपराधिक संहिता है और सभी आपराधिक विधियों को नागरिक संहिता से प्रतिस्थापित नहीं करती; प्रक्रिया तथा साक्ष्य के लिए BNSS एवं BSA हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि दंड के रूप में सामुदायिक सेवा BNS का प्रमुख परिवर्तन है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000074914","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Who was India’s first Olympic Gold medalist? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के प्रथम ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक विजेता कौन थे? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajyavardhan Singh Rathore","hi":"राज्यवर्धन सिंह राठौड़"},"2":{"en":"Abhinav Bindra","hi":"अभिनव बिंद्रा"},"3":{"en":"Sushil Kumar","hi":"सुशील कुमार"},"4":{"en":"Vijender Singh","hi":"विजेंद्र सिंह"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Abhinav Bindra</b><br><b>Abhinav Bindra</b> became India's first <b>individual Olympic gold medallist</b> by winning the <b>10 m air rifle</b> event at the <b>Beijing Olympics in 2008</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India's first Olympic medals as a team were the <b>gold in hockey at Amsterdam 1928</b>, but in an individual event the first gold was Bindra's.<br>• <b>Rajyavardhan Singh Rathore</b> won silver in double trap at Athens 2004, India's first individual silver, and <b>Sushil Kumar</b> and <b>Vijender Singh</b> won bronze at Beijing 2008.<br>• <b>Neeraj Chopra</b> won India's second individual gold in javelin at Tokyo 2020.<br>• Bindra also won the <b>World Championship gold in 2006</b> and received the Rajiv Gandhi Khel Ratna and Padma Bhushan.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Abhinav Bindra was India's first individual Olympic gold medallist.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अभिनव बिंद्रा</b><br><b>अभिनव बिंद्रा (Abhinav Bindra)</b> <b>2008 के बीजिंग ओलंपिक</b> में <b>10 मीटर एयर राइफल</b> स्पर्धा जीतकर भारत के <b>प्रथम व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक विजेता</b> बने।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत का प्रथम ओलंपिक पदक टीम के रूप में <b>1928 के एम्सटर्डम ओलंपिक में हॉकी का स्वर्ण</b> था, परंतु व्यक्तिगत स्पर्धा में पहला स्वर्ण बिंद्रा का था।<br>• <b>राज्यवर्धन सिंह राठौड़</b> ने एथेंस 2004 में डबल ट्रैप में रजत जीता, जो भारत का प्रथम व्यक्तिगत रजत था, तथा <b>सुशील कुमार</b> एवं <b>विजेंद्र सिंह</b> ने बीजिंग 2008 में कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>नीरज चोपड़ा</b> ने टोक्यो 2020 में भाला फेंक में भारत का दूसरा व्यक्तिगत स्वर्ण जीता।<br>• बिंद्रा ने <b>2006 में विश्व चैंपियनशिप स्वर्ण</b> भी जीता और उन्हें राजीव गांधी खेल रत्न तथा पद्म भूषण मिला।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि अभिनव बिंद्रा भारत के प्रथम व्यक्तिगत ओलंपिक स्वर्ण पदक विजेता थे।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000074915","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Prime Minister and Council of Ministers","question":{"en":"Who among the following is the longest serving Prime Minister of India? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन भारत के सबसे लंबे समय तक सेवा करने वाले प्रधानमंत्री हैं? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Manmohan Singh","hi":"मनमोहन सिंह"},"2":{"en":"Jawaharlal Nehru","hi":"जवाहरलाल नेहरू"},"3":{"en":"Narendra Modi","hi":"नरेंद्र मोदी"},"4":{"en":"Indira Gandhi","hi":"इंदिरा गांधी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Jawaharlal Nehru</b><br><b>Jawaharlal Nehru</b> is India's <b>longest-serving Prime Minister</b>, holding office for about <b>16 years and 286 days</b> from 15 August 1947 until 27 May 1964.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Nehru won <b>four general elections</b> (1952, 1957, 1962 and the first interim period) and was the first Prime Minister of India.<br>• <b>Indira Gandhi</b> served about 16 years in two terms (1966-77 and 1980-84) and is the longest-serving woman Prime Minister.<br>• <b>Manmohan Singh</b> served from 2004 to 2014, and <b>Narendra Modi</b> has been in office since 2014 and is the longest-serving non-Congress Prime Minister.<br>• The Prime Minister is appointed by the <b>President under Article 75</b> and is the head of the Council of Ministers.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Jawaharlal Nehru served longest as Prime Minister.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – जवाहरलाल नेहरू</b><br><b>जवाहरलाल नेहरू</b> भारत के <b>सबसे लंबे समय तक सेवा करने वाले प्रधानमंत्री</b> हैं, जिन्होंने 15 अगस्त 1947 से 27 मई 1964 तक लगभग <b>16 वर्ष 286 दिन</b> पद संभाला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नेहरू ने <b>चार आम चुनाव</b> (1952, 1957, 1962 तथा प्रथम अंतरिम काल) जीते और वे भारत के प्रथम प्रधानमंत्री थे।<br>• <b>इंदिरा गांधी</b> ने दो कार्यकालों (1966-77 तथा 1980-84) में लगभग 16 वर्ष सेवा की और सबसे लंबे समय तक पद पर रहने वाली महिला प्रधानमंत्री हैं।<br>• <b>मनमोहन सिंह</b> 2004 से 2014 तक रहे, तथा <b>नरेंद्र मोदी</b> 2014 से पद पर हैं और सबसे लंबे समय तक सेवा करने वाले गैर-कांग्रेसी प्रधानमंत्री हैं।<br>• प्रधानमंत्री की नियुक्ति <b>अनुच्छेद 75 के अंतर्गत राष्ट्रपति</b> करता है और वे मंत्रिपरिषद के प्रमुख होते हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि जवाहरलाल नेहरू ने सबसे लंबे समय तक प्रधानमंत्री रहकर सेवा की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000074916","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements is CORRECT about 'Deepor Beel'? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"'दीपोर बील' के बारे में निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन सही है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It is a man made lake located in the state of Assam.","hi":"यह असम राज्य में स्थित एक मानव-निर्मित झील है।"},"2":{"en":"It is located in former channel of the Manas River.","hi":"यह मानस नदी के पूर्ववर्ती चैनल में स्थित है।"},"3":{"en":"The Kalmani and Basistha rivers are their main water sources.","hi":"कलमणि तथा बसिष्ठ नदियाँ इसके मुख्य जल-स्रोत हैं।"},"4":{"en":"It is a wetland that is being considered for Ramsar site designation.","hi":"यह एक आर्द्रभूमि है जिसे रामसर स्थल के रूप में नामित किए जाने पर विचार किया जा रहा है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Kalmani and Basistha rivers are their main water sources.</b><br><b>Deepor Beel</b>, a major wetland near Guwahati, is fed mainly by the <b>Kalmani and Basistha rivers</b> along with the Brahmaputra, which makes statement (3) the correct one.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Deepor Beel is <b>not man-made</b>; it is a natural, oxbow-type wetland and remains the only <b>Ramsar site in Assam</b>, designated in 2002.<br>• It lies on a former channel of the <b>Brahmaputra</b>, not the Manas river, so statement (2) is wrong.<br>• It is an <b>Important Bird Area</b> with over 200 bird species and is a habitat of the endangered <b>greater adjutant stork</b>.<br>• The wetland is threatened by the Boragaon landfill, railway lines and urban expansion of Guwahati.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the Kalmani and Basistha are its main water sources.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कलमणि तथा बसिष्ठ नदियाँ इसके मुख्य जल-स्रोत हैं।</b><br>गुवाहाटी के निकट एक प्रमुख आर्द्रभूमि <b>दीपोर बील</b> को मुख्य रूप से <b>कलमणि तथा बसिष्ठ नदियों</b> के साथ ब्रह्मपुत्र से जल मिलता है, इसलिए कथन (3) सही है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दीपोर बील <b>मानव-निर्मित नहीं</b> है; यह प्राकृतिक, गोखुर (oxbow) प्रकार की आर्द्रभूमि है और असम का एकमात्र <b>रामसर स्थल</b> है, जिसे 2002 में नामित किया गया।<br>• यह <b>ब्रह्मपुत्र</b> की पूर्ववर्ती चैनल पर स्थित है, मानस नदी की नहीं, इसलिए कथन (2) गलत है।<br>• यह 200 से अधिक पक्षी प्रजातियों वाला <b>महत्वपूर्ण पक्षी क्षेत्र</b> है और संकटग्रस्त <b>बड़ा सहचर (ग्रेटर एडजुटेंट) सारस</b> का आवास है।<br>• इस आर्द्रभूमि को बोरागाँव कचरा भराव क्षेत्र, रेल लाइनों तथा गुवाहाटी के शहरी विस्तार से खतरा है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि कलमणि तथा बसिष्ठ इसके मुख्य जल-स्रोत हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000074917","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which statement about India’s performance at the 2023 Commonwealth Youth Games in Trinbago is <b>true</b>? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिनबागो में 2023 राष्ट्रमंडल युवा खेलों में भारत के प्रदर्शन के बारे में कौन-सा कथन <b>सही</b> है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"India won five medals: two silver and three bronze.","hi":"भारत ने पाँच पदक जीते: दो रजत तथा तीन कांस्य।"},"2":{"en":"India won medals only in swimming and netball.","hi":"भारत ने केवल तैराकी तथा नेटबॉल में पदक जीते।"},"3":{"en":"India competed in rugby sevens and beach volleyball only.","hi":"भारत ने केवल रग्बी सेवन्स तथा बीच वॉलीबॉल में भाग लिया।"},"4":{"en":"Shoan Ganguly won bronze in men’s 400m individual medley swimming.","hi":"शोआन गांगुली ने पुरुषों की 400 मीटर व्यक्तिगत मेडले तैराकी में कांस्य जीता।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – India won five medals: two silver and three bronze.</b><br>At the <b>2023 Commonwealth Youth Games in Trinbago</b> (Trinidad and Tobago), India won <b>five medals – two silver and three bronze</b>, all in athletics and swimming.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India's medallists included <b>Shivnarayan Pahal</b>, <b>Anushka Dattatray</b> and <b>Shashank Patil</b> in athletics, and <b>Vishal Grewal</b> and <b>Palak Joshi</b> in swimming.<br>• The Games were held in August 2023 in Trinidad and Tobago, with athletes aged 14-18 participating.<br>• India did not compete only in rugby sevens and beach volleyball, and won medals beyond swimming and netball, so options (2) and (3) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because India's tally at Trinbago 2023 was five medals – two silver and three bronze.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारत ने पाँच पदक जीते: दो रजत तथा तीन कांस्य।</b><br><b>त्रिनबागो (त्रिनिदाद एवं टोबैगो) में 2023 राष्ट्रमंडल युवा खेलों</b> में भारत ने <b>पाँच पदक – दो रजत तथा तीन कांस्य</b> जीते, जो सभी एथलेटिक्स तथा तैराकी में थे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत के पदक विजेताओं में एथलेटिक्स में <b>शिवनारायण पहल</b>, <b>अनुष्का दत्तात्रेय</b> तथा <b>शशांक पाटिल</b>, और तैराकी में <b>विशाल ग्रेवाल</b> एवं <b>पालक जोशी</b> सम्मिलित रहे।<br>• ये खेल अगस्त 2023 में त्रिनिदाद एवं टोबैगो में हुए, जिनमें 14-18 वर्ष के खिलाड़ियों ने भाग लिया।<br>• भारत ने केवल रग्बी सेवन्स तथा बीच वॉलीबॉल में भाग नहीं लिया, और तैराकी एवं नेटबॉल से आगे भी पदक जीते, इसलिए विकल्प (2) तथा (3) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि त्रिनबागो 2023 में भारत का पदक-स्कोर पाँच पदक – दो रजत तथा तीन कांस्य था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000074918","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements <b>accurately</b> describes the book 'Centres of Power: My Years in the Prime Minister's Office and Security Council'? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन पुस्तक 'सेंटर्स ऑफ पावर: माई इयर्स इन द प्राइम मिनिस्टर ऑफिस एंड सिक्योरिटी काउंसिल' का <b>सटीक</b> वर्णन करता है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Diplomatic memoir on India’s foreign policy","hi":"भारत की विदेश नीति पर कूटनीतिक संस्मरण"},"2":{"en":"Fictional tale of post-independence politics","hi":"स्वतंत्रता-पश्चात राजनीति की काल्पनिक कथा"},"3":{"en":"Biography of Indian Prime Ministers’ policies","hi":"भारतीय प्रधानमंत्रियों की नीतियों की जीवनी"},"4":{"en":"Collection of parliamentary speeches","hi":"संसदीय भाषणों का संग्रह"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Diplomatic memoir on India’s foreign policy</b><br><b>'Centres of Power: My Years in the Prime Minister's Office and Security Council'</b> is a <b>diplomatic memoir</b> by <b>Shivshankar Menon</b>, a former National Security Adviser and Foreign Secretary, dealing with India's foreign policy and security decision-making.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Shivshankar Menon served as <b>Foreign Secretary (2006-09)</b>, <b>National Security Adviser (2010-14)</b> and India's Ambassador to China.<br>• The memoir covers India's handling of issues such as the <b>India-US civil nuclear deal, the China relationship and Pakistan</b>.<br>• It is non-fiction and not a novel, biography or a collection of parliamentary speeches, so options (2), (3) and (4) are wrong.<br>• Menon's other book is <b>'Choices: Inside the Making of India's Foreign Policy'</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because the book is a diplomatic memoir on India's foreign policy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भारत की विदेश नीति पर कूटनीतिक संस्मरण</b><br><b>'सेंटर्स ऑफ पावर: माई इयर्स इन द प्राइम मिनिस्टर ऑफिस एंड सिक्योरिटी काउंसिल'</b> पूर्व राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार तथा विदेश सचिव <b>शिवशंकर मेनन</b> का <b>कूटनीतिक संस्मरण</b> है, जो भारत की विदेश नीति तथा सुरक्षा-निर्णय प्रक्रिया से संबंधित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• शिवशंकर मेनन <b>विदेश सचिव (2006-09)</b>, <b>राष्ट्रीय सुरक्षा सलाहकार (2010-14)</b> तथा चीन में भारत के राजदूत रहे।<br>• यह संस्मरण <b>भारत-अमेरिका असैन्य परमाणु समझौते, चीन से संबंध तथा पाकिस्तान</b> जैसे विषयों पर भारत के रुख को समेटता है।<br>• यह गैर-काल्पनिक कृति है, उपन्यास, जीवनी या संसदीय भाषणों का संग्रह नहीं, इसलिए विकल्प (2), (3) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br>• मेनन की दूसरी पुस्तक <b>'चॉइसेस: इनसाइड द मेकिंग ऑफ इंडियाज फॉरेन पॉलिसी'</b> है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि पुस्तक भारत की विदेश नीति पर कूटनीतिक संस्मरण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000074919","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Fundamental Rights","question":{"en":"Which article of the Constitution is called the 'Heart and Soul' by Dr. B.R. Ambedkar? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद को डॉ. बी. आर. आंबेडकर ने 'हृदय तथा आत्मा' कहा है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 20","hi":"अनुच्छेद 20"},"2":{"en":"Article 19","hi":"अनुच्छेद 19"},"3":{"en":"Article 32","hi":"अनुच्छेद 32"},"4":{"en":"Article 14","hi":"अनुच्छेद 14"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 32</b><br>Dr B.R. Ambedkar called <b>Article 32</b>, which gives the right to move the Supreme Court for enforcement of fundamental rights, the <b>'heart and soul of the Constitution'</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Article 32 makes the Supreme Court the <b>guarantor and protector</b> of fundamental rights and empowers it to issue writs of habeas corpus, mandamus, prohibition, quo warranto and certiorari.<br>• Article 32 itself is a <b>fundamental right</b> under Part III, and the Supreme Court cannot refuse relief under it.<br>• <b>Article 226</b> gives similar power to the High Courts, but it is not a fundamental right and is wider in scope.<br>• Article 19 protects six freedoms including speech and expression, Article 20 gives protection in respect of conviction and Article 14 guarantees equality before law.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Article 32 is called the heart and soul of the Constitution.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 32</b><br>डॉ. बी. आर. आंबेडकर ने <b>अनुच्छेद 32</b> को, जो मूल अधिकारों के प्रवर्तन के लिए सर्वोच्च न्यायालय जाने का अधिकार देता है, <b>'संविधान का हृदय तथा आत्मा'</b> कहा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 32 सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को मूल अधिकारों का <b>प्रत्याभूतिकर्ता तथा संरक्षक</b> बनाता है और उसे बंदी प्रत्यक्षीकरण, परमादेश, प्रतिषेध, अधिकार पृच्छा तथा उत्प्रेषण रिट जारी करने की शक्ति देता है।<br>• अनुच्छेद 32 स्वयं भाग III के अंतर्गत एक <b>मूल अधिकार</b> है और सर्वोच्च न्यायालय इसके अंतर्गत राहत देने से इनकार नहीं कर सकता।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 226</b> उच्च न्यायालयों को समान शक्ति देता है, परंतु वह मूल अधिकार नहीं है और उसका दायरा व्यापक है।<br>• अनुच्छेद 19 छह स्वतंत्रताओं की रक्षा करता है, अनुच्छेद 20 सिद्धदोष होने पर संरक्षण देता है तथा अनुच्छेद 14 विधि के समक्ष समता की गारंटी देता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि अनुच्छेद 32 को संविधान का हृदय तथा आत्मा कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000074920","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"Arrange the following dynasties in the <b>correct</b> chronological order in which they ruled Delhi:<br>1.Khalji<br>2.Lodi<br>3.Sayyid<br>4.Slave [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित राजवंशों को दिल्ली पर शासन के <b>सही</b> कालानुक्रम में व्यवस्थित करें:<br>1. खिलजी<br>2. लोदी<br>3. सैय्यद<br>4. गुलाम [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1, 2, 4, 3"},"2":{"en":"1, 2, 3, 4"},"3":{"en":"2, 3, 4, 1"},"4":{"en":"4, 1, 3, 2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 4, 1, 3, 2</b><br>The correct chronological order of the dynasties of the Delhi Sultanate is <b>Slave (1206-1290), Khalji (1290-1320), Tughlaq (1320-1414), Sayyid (1414-1451) and Lodi (1451-1526)</b>, so the order of the given names is <b>Slave – Khalji – Sayyid – Lodi</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Slave dynasty was founded by <b>Qutb-ud-din Aibak in 1206</b>, and the Khalji dynasty by <b>Jalal-ud-din Khalji in 1290</b>.<br>• The Sayyid dynasty was founded by <b>Khizr Khan in 1414</b>, and the Lodi dynasty by <b>Bahlol Lodi in 1451</b>.<br>• The Tughlaq dynasty, not mentioned in the list, ruled between the Khaljis and the Sayyids.<br>• The Delhi Sultanate ended with <b>Ibrahim Lodi's defeat at the First Battle of Panipat in 1526</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the order Slave – Khalji – Sayyid – Lodi is correct.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 4, 1, 3, 2</b><br>दिल्ली सल्तनत के राजवंशों का सही कालानुक्रम है – <b>गुलाम (1206-1290), खिलजी (1290-1320), तुगलक (1320-1414), सैय्यद (1414-1451) तथा लोदी (1451-1526)</b>, इसलिए दिए गए नामों का क्रम <b>गुलाम – खिलजी – सैय्यद – लोदी</b> होगा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गुलाम वंश की स्थापना <b>1206 में कुतुबुद्दीन ऐबक</b> ने तथा खिलजी वंश की स्थापना <b>1290 में जलालुद्दीन खिलजी</b> ने की।<br>• सैय्यद वंश की स्थापना <b>1414 में खिज्र खाँ</b> ने तथा लोदी वंश की स्थापना <b>1451 में बहलोल लोदी</b> ने की।<br>• सूची में उल्लिखित न होने वाला तुगलक वंश खिलजी तथा सैय्यद के बीच शासित रहा।<br>• दिल्ली सल्तनत का अंत <b>1526 में प्रथम पानीपत युद्ध में इब्राहिम लोदी की पराजय</b> से हुआ।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि गुलाम – खिलजी – सैय्यद – लोदी का क्रम सही है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000074921","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Maurya Dynasty","question":{"en":"Where is the Mauryan rock-cut architecture known as the Lomasa Rishi cave located in modern India ? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मौर्यकालीन शैलकृत वास्तुकला 'लोमस ऋषि गुफा' आधुनिक भारत में कहाँ स्थित है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ajanta caves","hi":"अजंता गुफाएँ"},"2":{"en":"Ellora caves","hi":"एलोरा गुफाएँ"},"3":{"en":"Barabar hills","hi":"बराबर पहाड़ियाँ"},"4":{"en":"Udayagiri hills","hi":"उदयगिरि पहाड़ियाँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Barabar hills</b><br>The <b>Lomasa Rishi cave</b>, a rock-cut cave with a polished interior and a decorated doorway, is located in the <b>Barabar hills</b> near Gaya in Bihar and belongs to the <b>Mauryan period</b>, dedicated by Ashoka.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Barabar caves, the <b>oldest surviving rock-cut caves in India</b>, include the Lomas Rishi, Sudama, Karn Chaupar and Visvakarma caves.<br>• The Lomasa Rishi doorway shows an elephant and stupa relief and is regarded as a precursor of the <b>chaitya arch</b> of later Buddhist architecture.<br>• The caves were used by the <b>Ajivika sect</b> and bear Ashokan inscriptions; the Mauryan polish on their granite walls is famous.<br>• <b>Ajanta and Ellora</b> belong to the Buddhist, Hindu and Jain cave traditions of the later period, and Udayagiri in Odisha is known for its Jain and Hindu caves.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the Lomasa Rishi cave is in the Barabar hills.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बराबर पहाड़ियाँ</b><br><b>लोमस ऋषि गुफा</b>, जिसका भीतरी भाग पॉलिशयुक्त तथा प्रवेशद्वार अलंकृत है, बिहार में गया के निकट <b>बराबर पहाड़ियों</b> में स्थित है और <b>मौर्य काल</b> की है, जिसे अशोक ने समर्पित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बराबर की गुफाएँ, जो <b>भारत की प्राचीनतम शेष शैलकृत गुफाएँ</b> हैं, लोमस ऋषि, सुदामा, कर्ण चौपार तथा विश्वकर्मा गुफाओं को सम्मिलित करती हैं।<br>• लोमस ऋषि के प्रवेशद्वार पर हाथी तथा स्तूप की उत्कीर्णन है और इसे परवर्ती बौद्ध वास्तुकला के <b>चैत्य मेहराब</b> का पूर्वरूप माना जाता है।<br>• इन गुफाओं का उपयोग <b>आजीविक संप्रदाय</b> करता था और इन पर अशोक के अभिलेख हैं; इनकी ग्रेनाइट दीवारों की मौर्य पॉलिश प्रसिद्ध है।<br>• <b>अजंता तथा एलोरा</b> परवर्ती काल की बौद्ध, हिंदू एवं जैन गुफा परंपरा की हैं, और ओडिशा का उदयगिरि जैन एवं हिंदू गुफाओं के लिए प्रसिद्ध है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि लोमस ऋषि गुफा बराबर पहाड़ियों में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000074922","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: State Legislature","question":{"en":"What must the Legislative Assembly do, according to Article 178 of the Indian Constitution, if the office of the Speaker or Deputy Speaker becomes vacant? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अनुच्छेद 178 के अनुसार यदि विधान सभा में अध्यक्ष या उपाध्यक्ष का पद रिक्त हो जाए तो विधान सभा को क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Request the Governor to appoint a temporary officer","hi":"रिक्त पद पर अस्थायी अधिकारी नियुक्त करने के लिए राज्यपाल से अनुरोध करना"},"2":{"en":"Leave the post vacant until the next general election","hi":"अगले आम चुनाव तक पद रिक्त रखना"},"3":{"en":"Choose another Assembly member to fill the vacancy","hi":"रिक्त स्थान भरने के लिए सभा के किसी अन्य सदस्य का चयन करना"},"4":{"en":"Transfer the duties to the Chairman of the Council","hi":"कर्तव्य परिषद के सभापति को हस्तांतरित करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Choose another Assembly member to fill the vacancy</b><br>Under <b>Article 178</b> of the Constitution, while the office of Speaker is vacant the duties are performed by the Deputy Speaker, and if both offices are vacant, the Legislative Assembly must <b>choose another of its members</b> to perform the duties of the Speaker.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Speaker and Deputy Speaker of a state assembly are elected by the <b>members of the Assembly</b> themselves under Article 178, mirroring Article 93 for the Lok Sabha.<br>• They hold office during the life of the Assembly and may be removed by a <b>majority of all the then members</b> of the House.<br>• The Speaker remains in office even after the dissolution of the Assembly until immediately before the first meeting of the new House.<br>• The Governor does not appoint a temporary officer and the duties are not transferred to the Legislative Council chairman, so options (1) and (4) are wrong.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the Assembly chooses another member to fill the vacancy.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रिक्त स्थान भरने के लिए सभा के किसी अन्य सदस्य का चयन करना</b><br>संविधान के <b>अनुच्छेद 178</b> के अंतर्गत अध्यक्ष का पद रिक्त होने पर कर्तव्य उपाध्यक्ष द्वारा निभाए जाते हैं, और यदि दोनों पद रिक्त हों तो विधान सभा को अध्यक्ष के कर्तव्यों के निर्वहन हेतु <b>अपने किसी अन्य सदस्य का चयन</b> करना होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• राज्य विधान सभा के अध्यक्ष तथा उपाध्यक्ष का चयन अनुच्छेद 178 के अंतर्गत <b>सभा के सदस्य</b> स्वयं करते हैं, जो लोकसभा के अनुच्छेद 93 के समान है।<br>• वे सभा के कार्यकाल तक पद पर रहते हैं और सदन के <b>तत्कालीन सदस्यों के बहुमत</b> से हटाए जा सकते हैं।<br>• विधान सभा के विघटन के बाद भी अध्यक्ष नई सभा की पहली बैठक से ठीक पहले तक पद पर रहते हैं।<br>• राज्यपाल अस्थायी अधिकारी नियुक्त नहीं करता और कर्तव्य विधान परिषद के सभापति को हस्तांतरित नहीं होते, इसलिए विकल्प (1) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि सभा रिक्त स्थान भरने हेतु किसी अन्य सदस्य का चयन करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000074923","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Which Constitutional Amendment Act inserted Article 239AA, providing special provisions for the Union Territory of Delhi? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम ने अनुच्छेद 239AA जोड़कर दिल्ली के केंद्रशासित प्रदेश के लिए विशेष प्रावधान किए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"61st Amendment Act, 1988","hi":"61वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम, 1988"},"2":{"en":"69th Amendment Act, 1991","hi":"69वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम, 1991"},"3":{"en":"73rd Amendment Act, 1992","hi":"73वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम, 1992"},"4":{"en":"91st Amendment Act, 2003","hi":"91वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम, 2003"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 69th Amendment Act, 1991</b><br>The <b>69th Constitutional Amendment Act, 1991</b> inserted <b>Article 239AA</b>, which gave special provisions to the Union Territory of Delhi, including a Legislative Assembly and a Council of Ministers, and re-designated it as the <b>National Capital Territory of Delhi</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The amendment came into force on <b>1 February 1992</b> and also inserted Articles 239AB and 239B and the 70th amendment?<br>• Delhi's Legislative Assembly can legislate on State List and Concurrent List subjects except <b>public order, police and land</b>.<br>• The <b>Government of NCT of Delhi Act, 1991</b> was passed to give effect to these provisions.<br>• The <b>61st Amendment (1988)</b> reduced the voting age to 18, the <b>73rd (1992)</b> dealt with panchayats and the <b>91st (2003)</b> with the size of the Council of Ministers.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because Article 239AA was inserted by the 69th Amendment.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 69वाँ संशोधन अधिनियम, 1991</b><br><b>69वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 1991</b> ने <b>अनुच्छेद 239AA</b> जोड़ा, जिसने दिल्ली के केंद्रशासित प्रदेश को विधान सभा तथा मंत्रिपरिषद सहित विशेष प्रावधान दिए और इसे <b>राष्ट्रीय राजधानी क्षेत्र दिल्ली</b> कहा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह संशोधन <b>1 फरवरी 1992</b> से प्रभावी हुआ और इसने अनुच्छेद 239AB तथा 239B भी जोड़े।<br>• दिल्ली की विधान सभा राज्य सूची तथा समवर्ती सूची के विषयों पर विधान बना सकती है, परंतु <b>लोक व्यवस्था, पुलिस तथा भूमि</b> को छोड़कर।<br>• इन प्रावधानों को क्रियान्वित करने के लिए <b>राष्ट्रीय राजधानी क्षेत्र दिल्ली सरकार अधिनियम, 1991</b> पारित हुआ।<br>• <b>61वाँ संशोधन (1988)</b> मताधिकार की आयु 18 वर्ष करने से, <b>73वाँ (1992)</b> पंचायतों से तथा <b>91वाँ (2003)</b> मंत्रिपरिषद के आकार से संबंधित था।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि अनुच्छेद 239AA 69वें संशोधन से जोड़ा गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000074924","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"In India, which crop is grown in the Zaid season? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में ज़ायद मौसम में कौन-सी फसल उगाई जाती है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Fodder","hi":"चारा"},"2":{"en":"Wheat","hi":"गेहूँ"},"3":{"en":"Jute","hi":"जूट"},"4":{"en":"Jowar","hi":"ज्वार"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Fodder</b><br>The <b>Zaid season</b> is the short summer cropping season between the rabi harvest and the kharif sowing (March to June), during which <b>fodder crops</b>, along with watermelon, muskmelon, cucumber, bitter gourd and moong, are grown on irrigated land.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India has three cropping seasons – <b>kharif (June-October), rabi (October-March) and zaid (March-June)</b>.<br>• <b>Wheat</b> is a rabi crop, while <b>jute and jowar</b> are kharif crops.<br>• Zaid crops mature quickly and need assured irrigation, and they help in the intensive use of land.<br>• Other zaid crops include <b>watermelon, musk melon, cucumber, pumpkin and green gram</b>.<br><b>Correct option = (1)</b>, because fodder is a crop of the Zaid season.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – चारा</b><br><b>ज़ायद मौसम</b> रबी की कटाई तथा खरीफ की बुवाई के बीच का छोटा ग्रीष्मकालीन फसल मौसम (मार्च से जून) है, जिसमें सिंचित भूमि पर <b>चारा फसलों</b> के साथ तरबूज़, खरबूज़ा, ककड़ी, करेला तथा मूँग उगाए जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में तीन फसल मौसम हैं – <b>खरीफ (जून-अक्टूबर), रबी (अक्टूबर-मार्च) तथा ज़ायद (मार्च-जून)</b>।<br>• <b>गेहूँ</b> रबी की फसल है, जबकि <b>जूट तथा ज्वार</b> खरीफ की फसलें हैं।<br>• ज़ायद की फसलें जल्दी पकती हैं और उन्हें सुनिश्चित सिंचाई चाहिए; ये भूमि के गहन उपयोग में सहायक हैं।<br>• अन्य ज़ायद फसलों में <b>तरबूज़, खरबूज़ा, ककड़ी, कद्दू तथा मूँग</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (1)</b>, क्योंकि चारा ज़ायद मौसम की फसल है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000074925","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"In which district of Odisha is the Bonai iron ore mine located? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बोनाई लोह अयस्क खदान ओडिशा के किस जिले में स्थित है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mayurbhanj","hi":"मयूरभंज"},"2":{"en":"Sundergarh","hi":"सुंदरगढ़"},"3":{"en":"Kendujhar","hi":"केंदुझर"},"4":{"en":"Singhbhum","hi":"सिंहभूम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Sundergarh</b><br>The <b>Bonai iron ore mine</b> is located in the <b>Bonai sub-division of Sundergarh district</b> in Odisha, in the iron-ore belt of the <b>Bonai-Keonjhar range</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Odisha is India's largest producer of <b>iron ore</b>, with major deposits in <b>Sundergarh, Keonjhar, Mayurbhanj and Jajpur</b> districts.<br>• The famous mines of the belt include <b>Barsua, Kalta, Koida, Kiriburu, Meghahatuburu, Gandhamardan and Malangtoli</b>.<br>• The <b>horse-shoe shaped BIF (banded iron formation)</b> of the Bonai-Keonjhar range supplies ore to plants such as Rourkela Steel Plant.<br>• <b>Singhbhum</b> is in Jharkhand, and <b>Mayurbhanj and Keonjhar</b> are other Odisha districts with iron ore, but Bonai lies in Sundergarh.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Bonai iron ore mine is in Sundergarh district.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सुंदरगढ़</b><br><b>बोनाई लोह अयस्क खदान</b> ओडिशा के <b>सुंदरगढ़ जिले के बोनाई उपखंड</b> में, <b>बोनाई-क्योंझर श्रेणी</b> की लोह-अयस्क पट्टी में स्थित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• ओडिशा भारत का सबसे बड़ा <b>लोह अयस्क</b> उत्पादक राज्य है, जिसके प्रमुख भंडार <b>सुंदरगढ़, क्योंझर, मयूरभंज तथा जाजपुर</b> जिलों में हैं।<br>• इस पट्टी की प्रसिद्ध खदानों में <b>बरसुआ, काल्टा, कोइडा, किरिबुरु, मेघाहातुबुरु, गंधमार्दन तथा मलांगतोली</b> सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• बोनाई-क्योंझर श्रेणी की <b>घोड़े की नाल आकार की BIF (पट्टित लौह संरचना)</b> राउरकेला इस्पात संयंत्र जैसे कारखानों को अयस्क देती है।<br>• <b>सिंहभूम</b> झारखंड में है, तथा <b>मयूरभंज एवं क्योंझर</b> ओडिशा के अन्य लोह-अयस्क जिले हैं, परंतु बोनाई सुंदरगढ़ में है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि बोनाई लोह अयस्क खदान सुंदरगढ़ जिले में है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000074926","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Under the Constitution of India, which authority has the power to enlarge the jurisdiction and powers of the Supreme Court with respect to matters in the Union List? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के अंतर्गत संघ सूची के विषयों के संबंध में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के क्षेत्राधिकार तथा शक्तियों का विस्तार करने की शक्ति किस प्राधिकारी को है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajya Sabha alone","hi":"केवल राज्यसभा"},"2":{"en":"Chief Justice of India","hi":"भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश"},"3":{"en":"Parliament of India","hi":"भारत की संसद"},"4":{"en":"President of India","hi":"भारत के राष्ट्रपति"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Parliament of India</b><br>Under <b>Article 138</b>, <b>Parliament</b> may by law enlarge the jurisdiction and powers of the Supreme Court with respect to any matter in the Union List, and may also confer further jurisdiction on matters arising under treaties.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Supreme Court's jurisdiction is set out in <b>Articles 131 to 140</b> – original, appellate, advisory (Article 143), writ (Article 32) and special leave (Article 136).<br>• Parliament can also confer <b>supplemental powers</b> on the Supreme Court under Article 138(2) and curtail some appellate jurisdiction under Article 138.<br>• The <b>Chief Justice of India</b> is the head of the judiciary but cannot enlarge jurisdiction, and the President acts only on the advice of the Council of Ministers.<br>• Article 138 reflects the principle that the Supreme Court's jurisdiction is <b>not fixed for all time</b> and may be expanded by legislation.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because Parliament has the power to enlarge the Supreme Court's jurisdiction.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भारत की संसद</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 138</b> के अंतर्गत <b>संसद</b> विधि द्वारा संघ सूची के किसी विषय के संबंध में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का क्षेत्राधिकार तथा शक्तियाँ बढ़ा सकती है, और संधियों से उत्पन्न विषयों पर भी अतिरिक्त क्षेत्राधिकार दे सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का क्षेत्राधिकार <b>अनुच्छेद 131 से 140</b> में दिया गया है – मूल, अपीलीय, परामर्शी (अनुच्छेद 143), रिट (अनुच्छेद 32) तथा विशेष अनुमति (अनुच्छेद 136)।<br>• संसद अनुच्छेद 138(2) के अंतर्गत सर्वोच्च न्यायालय को <b>पूरक शक्तियाँ</b> भी दे सकती है।<br>• <b>भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> न्यायपालिका के प्रमुख हैं परंतु क्षेत्राधिकार नहीं बढ़ा सकते, और राष्ट्रपति मंत्रिपरिषद की सलाह पर ही कार्य करता है।<br>• अनुच्छेद 138 इस सिद्धांत को दर्शाता है कि सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का क्षेत्राधिकार <b>सदा के लिए निश्चित नहीं</b> है और विधान द्वारा बढ़ाया जा सकता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का क्षेत्राधिकार बढ़ाने की शक्ति संसद के पास है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000074927","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A disciplinary authority conducting departmental arbitration proceedings records witness testimony and admits electronic evidence. One party argues that the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam 2023, in India automatically applies because evidence is being taken. Which of the following statements is legally correct? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक अनुशासनिक प्राधिकारी विभागीय मध्यस्थता कार्यवाही में गवाहों का परीक्षण रिकॉर्ड करता है तथा इलेक्ट्रॉनिक साक्ष्य ग्रहण करता है। एक पक्ष तर्क देता है कि भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023 (भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023) स्वतः लागू होता है क्योंकि साक्ष्य ग्रहण किया जा रहा है। निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Adhiniyam applies because all proceedings involving evidence are covered.","hi":"अधिनियम लागू होता है क्योंकि साक्ष्य सम्मिलित करने वाली सभी कार्यवाहियाँ इसके दायरे में हैं।"},"2":{"en":"The Adhiniyam applies only to criminal proceedings.","hi":"अधिनियम केवल आपराधिक कार्यवाहियों पर लागू होता है।"},"3":{"en":"The Adhiniyam does not apply to proceedings before an arbitrator.","hi":"अधिनियम मध्यस्थ के समक्ष कार्यवाहियों पर लागू नहीं होता।"},"4":{"en":"The Adhiniyam applies only if both parties consent.","hi":"अधिनियम केवल तभी लागू होता है जब दोनों पक्ष सहमति दें।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – The Adhiniyam does not apply to proceedings before an arbitrator.</b><br>Under the <b>Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam, 2023</b>, the Act applies to <b>proceedings before a court</b> and not to <b>arbitration or purely departmental proceedings</b> before a private arbitrator or disciplinary authority, so it does not apply merely because evidence is being recorded.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The BSA's scope is defined with reference to <b>judicial proceedings in or before a court</b>, and arbitration is governed by the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996.<br>• Departmental or arbitral tribunals follow their own procedure and the principles of natural justice, and the <b>Evidence Act does not bind them in its strict form</b>.<br>• The BSA is not limited to criminal proceedings and does not require the consent of parties for application, so options (2) and (4) are wrong.<br>• The BSA replaced the Indian Evidence Act, 1872 and expanded the scope of <b>electronic and digital evidence</b> under Sections 61-63.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the Adhiniyam does not apply to proceedings before an arbitrator.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अधिनियम मध्यस्थ के समक्ष कार्यवाहियों पर लागू नहीं होता।</b><br><b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 2023</b> के अंतर्गत यह अधिनियम <b>न्यायालय के समक्ष कार्यवाहियों</b> पर लागू होता है, न कि निजी मध्यस्थ या अनुशासनिक प्राधिकारी के समक्ष <b>मध्यस्थता या पूर्णतः विभागीय कार्यवाहियों</b> पर, इसलिए केवल साक्ष्य ग्रहण होने से यह लागू नहीं हो जाता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BSA का दायरा <b>न्यायालय में या उसके समक्ष न्यायिक कार्यवाहियों</b> के संदर्भ में निर्धारित है, और मध्यस्थता मध्यस्थता एवं सुलह अधिनियम, 1996 से नियंत्रित होती है।<br>• विभागीय या मध्यस्थ अधिकरण अपनी प्रक्रिया तथा नैसर्गिक न्याय के सिद्धांतों का पालन करते हैं, और <b>साक्ष्य अधिनियम उन्हें कठोर रूप में बाध्य नहीं करता</b>।<br>• BSA केवल आपराधिक कार्यवाहियों तक सीमित नहीं है और इसके प्रयोग हेतु पक्षों की सहमति आवश्यक नहीं, इसलिए विकल्प (2) तथा (4) गलत हैं।<br>• BSA ने भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम, 1872 का स्थान लिया और धारा 61-63 के अंतर्गत <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक एवं डिजिटल साक्ष्य</b> का दायरा बढ़ाया।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि अधिनियम मध्यस्थ के समक्ष कार्यवाहियों पर लागू नहीं होता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000074928","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"As part of the post-1991 economic reforms, what type of autonomy was granted to Maharatna, Navratna and Miniratna public sector enterprises? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के पश्चात आर्थिक सुधारों के अंग के रूप में महारत्न, नवरत्न तथा मिनीरत्न सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उद्यमों को किस प्रकार की स्वायत्तता दी गई? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Commercial, diplomatic and regulatory autonomy","hi":"वाणिज्यिक, कूटनीतिक तथा नियामक स्वायत्तता"},"2":{"en":"Administrative, judicial and legislative autonomy","hi":"प्रशासनिक, न्यायिक तथा विधायी स्वायत्तता"},"3":{"en":"Financial, political and constitutional autonomy","hi":"वित्तीय, राजनीतिक तथा संवैधानिक स्वायत्तता"},"4":{"en":"Financial, managerial and operational autonomy","hi":"वित्तीय, प्रबंधकीय तथा परिचालन स्वायत्तता"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Financial, managerial and operational autonomy</b><br>As part of the post-1991 reforms, <b>Maharatna, Navratna and Miniratna</b> public sector enterprises were granted greater <b>financial, managerial and operational autonomy</b>, allowing them to take investment and business decisions within enhanced delegated limits.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Navratna</b> status was introduced in 1997 and allows investment up to ₹1,000 crore without government approval; <b>Maharatna</b> status (2010) allows up to ₹5,000 crore.<br>• <b>Miniratna</b> enterprises (Category I and II) have lower investment ceilings and greater operational freedom.<br>• The classification seeks to make PSUs competitive and professional, with powers to form joint ventures, raise capital and enter global markets.<br>• These enterprises remain accountable to Parliament and are audited by the CAG, so the autonomy is not constitutional or judicial.<br><b>Correct option = (4)</b>, because the autonomy granted is financial, managerial and operational.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – वित्तीय, प्रबंधकीय तथा परिचालन स्वायत्तता</b><br>1991 के पश्चात सुधारों के अंग के रूप में <b>महारत्न, नवरत्न तथा मिनीरत्न</b> सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उद्यमों को अधिक <b>वित्तीय, प्रबंधकीय तथा परिचालन स्वायत्तता</b> दी गई, जिससे वे बढ़ी हुई प्रत्यायोजित सीमाओं में निवेश एवं व्यावसायिक निर्णय ले सकें।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नवरत्न</b> दर्जा 1997 में शुरू हुआ और सरकारी अनुमति के बिना ₹1,000 करोड़ तक निवेश की अनुमति देता है; <b>महारत्न</b> दर्जा (2010) ₹5,000 करोड़ तक की अनुमति देता है।<br>• <b>मिनीरत्न</b> उद्यमों (श्रेणी I तथा II) की निवेश सीमा कम है परंतु परिचालन स्वतंत्रता अधिक है।<br>• यह वर्गीकरण सार्वजनिक उद्यमों को प्रतिस्पर्धी एवं व्यावसायिक बनाना चाहता है, जिसमें संयुक्त उद्यम बनाने, पूँजी जुटाने तथा वैश्विक बाजारों में प्रवेश की शक्तियाँ हैं।<br>• ये उद्यम संसद के प्रति उत्तरदायी रहते हैं और CAG द्वारा लेखापरीक्षित होते हैं, इसलिए यह स्वायत्तता संवैधानिक या न्यायिक नहीं है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (4)</b>, क्योंकि दी गई स्वायत्तता वित्तीय, प्रबंधकीय तथा परिचालन की है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000074929","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"Two trains of equal length are moving on parallel tracks in opposite directions at speeds of 62 km/h (kilometers per hour) and 208 km/h (kilometers per hour). A passenger sitting in one train observes the other train pass completely in 15 seconds. What is the length of each train? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"समान लंबाई की दो रेलगाड़ियाँ समानांतर पटरियों पर विपरीत दिशाओं में 62 किमी/घंटा तथा 208 किमी/घंटा की चाल से चल रही हैं। एक रेलगाड़ी में बैठा यात्री देखता है कि दूसरी रेलगाड़ी 15 सेकंड में पूरी तरह निकल जाती है। प्रत्येक रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई कितनी है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"750 (meters)","hi":"750 मीटर"},"2":{"en":"900 (meters)","hi":"900 मीटर"},"3":{"en":"1,125 (meters)","hi":"1,125 मीटर"},"4":{"en":"1,250 (meters)","hi":"1,250 मीटर"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 1,125 (meters)</b><br>When two trains move in opposite directions, the <b>relative speed</b> is 62 + 208 = <b>270 km/h</b> = 270 × 5/18 = <b>75 m/s</b>, and in 15 seconds the distance covered is 75 × 15 = <b>1,125 m</b>, which equals the length of the other train (since the observer is a point).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A passenger in one train is treated as a <b>point</b>, so the distance covered equals the length of the other train only, which is the length of each train since they are equal.<br>• Conversion: <b>km/h × 5/18 = m/s</b>.<br>• If both trains had to cross each other fully, the distance would be the <b>sum of both lengths</b>.<br>• Time = distance / relative speed, so a higher relative speed gives a shorter crossing time.<br><b>Correct option = (3)</b>, because the length of each train is 1,125 metres.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1,125 मीटर</b><br>जब दो रेलगाड़ियाँ विपरीत दिशाओं में चलती हैं, तो <b>सापेक्ष चाल</b> 62 + 208 = <b>270 किमी/घंटा</b> = 270 × 5/18 = <b>75 मीटर/सेकंड</b> होती है, और 15 सेकंड में तय दूरी 75 × 15 = <b>1,125 मीटर</b> है, जो दूसरी रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई के बराबर है (क्योंकि प्रेक्षक एक बिंदु है)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एक रेलगाड़ी में बैठे यात्री को <b>बिंदु</b> माना जाता है, इसलिए तय दूरी केवल दूसरी रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई के बराबर होती है, और चूँकि दोनों समान लंबाई की हैं, यही प्रत्येक की लंबाई है।<br>• रूपांतरण: <b>किमी/घंटा × 5/18 = मीटर/सेकंड</b>।<br>• यदि दोनों रेलगाड़ियों को एक-दूसरे को पूरी तरह पार करना हो, तो दूरी <b>दोनों लंबाइयों का योग</b> होती।<br>• समय = दूरी / सापेक्ष चाल, इसलिए अधिक सापेक्ष चाल से पार होने का समय कम होता है।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (3)</b>, क्योंकि प्रत्येक रेलगाड़ी की लंबाई 1,125 मीटर है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000074930","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Governor-General and Viceroy","question":{"en":"During whose tenure was the Vernacular Press Act, which sought to restrict newspapers published in Indian languages, enacted? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वर्नाक्युलर प्रेस एक्ट, जो भारतीय भाषाओं में प्रकाशित समाचार-पत्रों को नियंत्रित करना चाहता था, किसके कार्यकाल में लागू किया गया? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lord Ripon","hi":"लॉर्ड रिपन"},"2":{"en":"Lord Lytton","hi":"लॉर्ड लिटन"},"3":{"en":"Lord Curzon","hi":"लॉर्ड कर्ज़न"},"4":{"en":"Lord Mayo","hi":"लॉर्ड मेयो"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Lord Lytton</b><br>The <b>Vernacular Press Act, 1878</b>, which sought to restrict newspapers published in Indian languages, was enacted during the tenure of <b>Lord Lytton</b> (1876-1880).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Act empowered the government to demand a bond from vernacular newspapers and to seize their presses for seditious writing, while English-language papers were exempt.<br>• It was repealed by <b>Lord Ripon in 1882</b>, who is known for his liberal measures such as the Ilbert Bill and local self-government.<br>• Lord Lytton also held the <b>Delhi Durbar of 1877</b>, passed the Arms Act and imposed the unpopular <b>cotton import duty</b> during the famine of 1876-78.<br>• <b>Lord Curzon</b> partitioned Bengal in 1905, and <b>Lord Mayo</b> was assassinated in 1872 at Port Blair.<br><b>Correct option = (2)</b>, because the Vernacular Press Act was enacted during Lord Lytton's tenure.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – लॉर्ड लिटन</b><br><b>वर्नाक्युलर प्रेस एक्ट, 1878</b>, जो भारतीय भाषाओं में प्रकाशित समाचार-पत्रों को नियंत्रित करना चाहता था, <b>लॉर्ड लिटन</b> (1876-1880) के कार्यकाल में लागू किया गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह अधिनियम सरकार को देशी भाषा के समाचार-पत्रों से बंधपत्र माँगने तथा राजद्रोही लेखन पर उनके प्रेस जब्त करने की शक्ति देता था, जबकि अंग्रेज़ी समाचार-पत्र इससे मुक्त थे।<br>• इसे <b>1882 में लॉर्ड रिपन</b> ने निरसित किया, जो इल्बर्ट बिल तथा स्थानीय स्वशासन जैसे उदार उपायों के लिए जाने जाते हैं।<br>• लॉर्ड लिटन ने <b>1877 का दिल्ली दरबार</b> भी आयोजित किया, शस्त्र अधिनियम पारित किया तथा 1876-78 के अकाल में अलोकप्रिय <b>सूती आयात शुल्क</b> लगाया।<br>• <b>लॉर्ड कर्ज़न</b> ने 1905 में बंगाल का विभाजन किया, और <b>लॉर्ड मेयो</b> की 1872 में पोर्ट ब्लेयर में हत्या कर दी गई।<br><b>सही विकल्प = (2)</b>, क्योंकि वर्नाक्युलर प्रेस एक्ट लॉर्ड लिटन के कार्यकाल में लागू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000074931","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A hollow metallic sphere has an outer radius of 4 cm and a thickness of 3 cm. Calculate the total volume of metal used to make the sphere. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक खोखले धातु के गोले की बाहरी त्रिज्या 4 cm और मोटाई 3 cm है। गोला बनाने में प्रयुक्त धातु का कुल आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"254 cm³"},"2":{"en":"354 cm³"},"3":{"en":"264 cm³"},"4":{"en":"246 cm³"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"192\" height=\"192\" viewBox=\"0 0 192 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 0 166 96\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 1 166 96M96 96L150 51M96 96L78 96\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"70\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"112\" y=\"64\">R = 4</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">r = 1</text></g></svg><br>Outer radius \\(R = 4\\) cm, inner radius \\(r = 4 - 3 = 1\\) cm<br>Volume of metal = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi(R^3 - r^3) = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times (64 - 1)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 63 = 4 \\times 22 \\times 3 = \\boxed{264}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 264 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"192\" height=\"192\" viewBox=\"0 0 192 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 0 166 96\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 1 166 96M96 96L150 51M96 96L78 96\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"70\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"112\" y=\"64\">R = 4</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">r = 1</text></g></svg><br>बाहरी त्रिज्या \\(R = 4\\) cm, आंतरिक त्रिज्या \\(r = 4 - 3 = 1\\) cm<br>धातु का आयतन = \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi(R^3 - r^3) = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times (64 - 1)\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 63 = 4 \\times 22 \\times 3 = \\boxed{264}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 264 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000074932","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"If l = 9 cm, b = 4 cm, and h = 2 cm, the volume is: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि l = 9 cm, b = 4 cm और h = 2 cm है, तो आयतन है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"72 cm³"},"2":{"en":"80 cm³"},"3":{"en":"68 cm³"},"4":{"en":"90 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"269\" height=\"112\" viewBox=\"-17 0 269 112\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 86L190 86M26 86L26 49M190 86L226 62M190 86L190 49M26 49L190 49M26 49L62 26M226 62L226 26M190 49L226 26M62 26L226 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 86L62 62M62 62L226 62M62 62L62 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"102\">9 cm</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"95\">4 cm</text><text x=\"2\" y=\"71\">2 cm</text></g></svg><br>Volume of a cuboid = \\(l \\times b \\times h\\)<br>\\(= 9 \\times 4 \\times 2 = \\boxed{72}\\) cm³<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 72 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"269\" height=\"112\" viewBox=\"-17 0 269 112\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 86L190 86M26 86L26 49M190 86L226 62M190 86L190 49M26 49L190 49M26 49L62 26M226 62L226 26M190 49L226 26M62 26L226 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 86L62 62M62 62L226 62M62 62L62 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"108\" y=\"102\">9 cm</text><text x=\"218\" y=\"95\">4 cm</text><text x=\"2\" y=\"71\">2 cm</text></g></svg><br>घनाभ का आयतन = \\(l \\times b \\times h\\)<br>\\(= 9 \\times 4 \\times 2 = \\boxed{72}\\) cm³<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 72 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000074933","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"If a : b = 2 : 3 and b : c = 4 : 5, find a² : b² : bc. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a : b = 2 : 3 और b : c = 4 : 5 है, तो a² : b² : bc ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"16:36:40"},"2":{"en":"16:36:45"},"3":{"en":"15:36:45"},"4":{"en":"16:30:45"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Make b common: b = LCM(3, 4) multiples → a : b = 8 : 12 and b : c = 12 : 15<br>So \\(a = 8,\\ b = 12,\\ c = 15\\)<br>\\(a^2 : b^2 : bc = 64 : 144 : 180 = \\boxed{16 : 36 : 45}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 16:36:45.</b>","hi":"b को समान कीजिए: a : b = 8 : 12 और b : c = 12 : 15<br>अतः \\(a = 8,\\ b = 12,\\ c = 15\\)<br>\\(a^2 : b^2 : bc = 64 : 144 : 180 = \\boxed{16 : 36 : 45}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 16:36:45 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000074934","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, angle A = 60°, AB = 6 cm, AC = 8 cm. What is the area of the triangle? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, कोण A = 60°, AB = 6 cm, AC = 8 cm है। त्रिभुज का क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12√3 cm²"},"2":{"en":"8√3 cm²"},"3":{"en":"10√3 cm²"},"4":{"en":"9√3 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"199\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 199 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L173 196ZM44 196A18 18 0 0 0 35 180\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"126\" y=\"16\">C</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"208\">A</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"209\">B</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"212\">6 cm</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"103\">8 cm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>Area = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\times AC \\times \\sin A\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times \\sin 60^\\circ = 24 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 12√3 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"199\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 199 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M124 26L26 196L173 196ZM44 196A18 18 0 0 0 35 180\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"126\" y=\"16\">C</text><text x=\"13\" y=\"208\">A</text><text x=\"185\" y=\"209\">B</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"212\">6 cm</text><text x=\"55\" y=\"103\">8 cm</text><text x=\"52\" y=\"185\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times AB \\times AC \\times \\sin A\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 \\times \\sin 60^\\circ = 24 \\times \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{12\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 12√3 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000074935","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A conical vessel has a height of 3.5 cm and can hold 3.3 litres of milk. What is the radius of its base? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंक्वाकार बर्तन की ऊँचाई 3.5 cm है और वह 3.3 लीटर दूध धारण कर सकता है। उसके आधार की त्रिज्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36 cm"},"2":{"en":"45 cm"},"3":{"en":"30 cm"},"4":{"en":"35 cm"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(3.3\\) litres = 3300 cm³<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 3300\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r^2 \\times 3.5 = 3300 \\Rightarrow \\frac{22 r^2}{6} = 3300\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 900 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{30}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 30 cm.</b>","hi":"\\(3.3\\) लीटर = 3300 cm³<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = 3300\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times r^2 \\times 3.5 = 3300 \\Rightarrow \\frac{22 r^2}{6} = 3300\\)<br>\\(r^2 = 900 \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{30}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 30 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000074936","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A person travels to a city at 12 km/hr and returns at 9 km/hr. If the total time taken is 7 hours, find the distance between the two places. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति किसी शहर तक 12 km/hr की चाल से जाता है और 9 km/hr की चाल से लौटता है। यदि कुल समय 7 घंटे है, तो दोनों स्थानों के बीच की दूरी ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"24 km"},"2":{"en":"36 km"},"3":{"en":"48 km"},"4":{"en":"54 km"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{d}{12} + \\frac{d}{9} = 7\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3d + 4d}{36} = 7 \\Rightarrow 7d = 252\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{36}\\) km<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 36 km.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{d}{12} + \\frac{d}{9} = 7\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3d + 4d}{36} = 7 \\Rightarrow 7d = 252\\)<br>\\(d = \\boxed{36}\\) km<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 36 km है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000074937","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{8^n} = 4096\\), then the value of n is: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{8^n} = 4096\\) है, तो n का मान है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(4096 = 2^{12}\\) and \\(\\sqrt{8^n} = 8^{n/2} = 2^{3n/2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3n}{2} = 12\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 8.</b>","hi":"\\(4096 = 2^{12}\\) और \\(\\sqrt{8^n} = 8^{n/2} = 2^{3n/2}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{3n}{2} = 12\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{8}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000074938","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{(0.75)^3-(0.25)^3}{0.5625+0.1875+0.0625}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\\(\\frac{(0.75)^3-(0.25)^3}{0.5625+0.1875+0.0625}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.2"},"2":{"en":"0.8"},"3":{"en":"0.6"},"4":{"en":"0.5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Using \\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) with \\(a = 0.75\\), \\(b = 0.25\\):<br>\\(a^2 = 0.5625\\), \\(ab = 0.1875\\), \\(b^2 = 0.0625\\), so the denominator is \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\)<br>Expression = \\(a - b = 0.75 - 0.25 = \\boxed{0.5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 0.5.</b>","hi":"\\(a^3 - b^3 = (a - b)(a^2 + ab + b^2)\\) का उपयोग, जहाँ \\(a = 0.75\\), \\(b = 0.25\\):<br>\\(a^2 = 0.5625\\), \\(ab = 0.1875\\), \\(b^2 = 0.0625\\), अतः हर \\(a^2 + ab + b^2\\) है<br>व्यंजक = \\(a - b = 0.75 - 0.25 = \\boxed{0.5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 0.5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000074939","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Find the remainder when 10¹ + 10² + 10³ + ... + 10¹⁰⁰ is divided by 6. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जब 10¹ + 10² + 10³ + ... + 10¹⁰⁰ को 6 से भाग दिया जाए तो शेषफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"8"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(10 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 6\\), so \\(10^k \\equiv 4^k\\)<br>\\(4^2 = 16 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 6\\), so every power of 10 leaves remainder 4<br>Sum of 100 such terms \\(\\equiv 100 \\times 4 = 400 \\equiv \\boxed{4} \\pmod 6\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.</b>","hi":"\\(10 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 6\\), अतः \\(10^k \\equiv 4^k\\)<br>\\(4^2 = 16 \\equiv 4 \\pmod 6\\), अतः 10 की प्रत्येक घात शेषफल 4 देती है<br>ऐसे 100 पदों का योग \\(\\equiv 100 \\times 4 = 400 \\equiv \\boxed{4} \\pmod 6\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000074940","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In ΔPQR, the medians intersect at centroid G. If the total length of median PD is 15 cm, what is the length of segment PG? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ΔPQR में, माध्यिकाएँ केंद्रक G पर प्रतिच्छेद करती हैं। यदि माध्यिका PD की कुल लंबाई 15 cm है, तो रेखाखंड PG की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7 cm"},"2":{"en":"13 cm"},"3":{"en":"8 cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"213\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 213\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M87 26L26 187L256 187ZM87 26L141 187M84 182l0 10M198 182l0 10\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"133\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"83\" y=\"17\">P</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"198\">Q</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"196\">R</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"198\">D</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"start\">G</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">?</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">PD = 15</text></g></svg><br>The centroid divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1, so \\(PG = \\frac{2}{3} \\times PD\\)<br>\\(PG = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 15 = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 10 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"213\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 213\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M87 26L26 187L256 187ZM87 26L141 187M84 182l0 10M198 182l0 10\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"133\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"83\" y=\"17\">P</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"198\">Q</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"196\">R</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"198\">D</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"start\">G</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">?</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">PD = 15</text></g></svg><br>केंद्रक प्रत्येक माध्यिका को 2 : 1 में विभाजित करता है, अतः \\(PG = \\frac{2}{3} \\times PD\\)<br>\\(PG = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 15 = \\boxed{10}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 10 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000074941","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If the ratio of the units digit to the tens digit of a two-digit number is 3:1. The sum of the digits is 8. What is the original number? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी दो अंकों की संख्या के इकाई अंक का दहाई अंक से अनुपात 3:1 है। अंकों का योग 8 है। मूल संख्या क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"32"},"3":{"en":"45"},"4":{"en":"26"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let tens digit = \\(x\\), units digit = \\(3x\\)<br>\\(x + 3x = 8 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>Number = \\(20 + 6 = \\boxed{26}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 26.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए दहाई अंक = \\(x\\), इकाई अंक = \\(3x\\)<br>\\(x + 3x = 8 \\Rightarrow x = 2\\)<br>संख्या = \\(20 + 6 = \\boxed{26}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 26 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000074942","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Ravi starts from his home towards school at 8:20 a.m. on a bicycle. If he travels at 10 km/h, he reaches the school 8 minutes late, whereas if he travels at 16 km/h, he arrives 10 minutes early. Determine the starting time of the school. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रवि सुबह 8:20 बजे साइकिल से घर से स्कूल के लिए निकलता है। यदि वह 10 km/h की चाल से चलता है तो स्कूल 8 मिनट देर से पहुँचता है, जबकि 16 km/h की चाल से 10 मिनट पहले पहुँच जाता है। स्कूल प्रारंभ होने का समय ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 : 50 am"},"2":{"en":"9 : 00 am"},"3":{"en":"9 : 20 am"},"4":{"en":"10 : 05 am"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Difference in time = \\(8 + 10 = 18\\) minutes = \\(\\frac{3}{10}\\) hour<br>\\(\\frac{d}{10} - \\frac{d}{16} = \\frac{3}{10} \\Rightarrow \\frac{8d - 5d}{80} = \\frac{3}{10} \\Rightarrow 3d = 24 \\Rightarrow d = 8\\) km<br>Time at 10 km/h = \\(\\frac{8}{10}\\) h = 48 min, so he reaches at 9:08 — that is 8 min late<br>School starts at \\(9{:}08 - 8\\) min = \\(\\boxed{9{:}00\\ \\text{am}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 9 : 00 am.</b>","hi":"समय का अंतर = \\(8 + 10 = 18\\) मिनट = \\(\\frac{3}{10}\\) घंटा<br>\\(\\frac{d}{10} - \\frac{d}{16} = \\frac{3}{10} \\Rightarrow \\frac{8d - 5d}{80} = \\frac{3}{10} \\Rightarrow 3d = 24 \\Rightarrow d = 8\\) km<br>10 km/h पर समय = \\(\\frac{8}{10}\\) घंटा = 48 मिनट, अतः वह 9:08 पर पहुँचता है — जो 8 मिनट देर है<br>स्कूल \\(9{:}08 - 8\\) मिनट = \\(\\boxed{9{:}00\\ \\text{am}}\\) पर शुरू होता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 9 : 00 am है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000074943","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A and B can complete the work in 9 days and 36 days, respectively. A starts the work and they work alternately, one person working each day. In how many days will the entire work be completed? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B किसी कार्य को क्रमशः 9 दिन और 36 दिन में पूरा कर सकते हैं। A कार्य शुरू करता है और वे बारी-बारी से, प्रतिदिन एक व्यक्ति कार्य करते हुए कार्य करते हैं। पूरा कार्य कितने दिनों में समाप्त होगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\) days","hi":"\\(12\\frac{1}{2}\\) दिन"},"2":{"en":"\\(9\\frac{1}{4}\\) days","hi":"\\(9\\frac{1}{4}\\) दिन"},"3":{"en":"\\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) days","hi":"\\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) दिन"},"4":{"en":"\\(18\\frac{1}{2}\\) days","hi":"\\(18\\frac{1}{2}\\) दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Work in one pair of days (A then B) = \\(\\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{36} = \\frac{5}{36}\\)<br>In 14 days (7 pairs) = \\(\\frac{35}{36}\\), leaving \\(\\frac{1}{36}\\)<br>On day 15 A works: A does \\(\\frac{1}{9}\\) per day, so the remaining work needs \\(\\frac{1/36}{1/9} = \\frac{1}{4}\\) day<br>Total = \\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) days = \\(\\boxed{14\\frac{1}{4}}\\) days<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) days.</b>","hi":"एक जोड़ी दिनों में कार्य (पहले A फिर B) = \\(\\frac{1}{9} + \\frac{1}{36} = \\frac{5}{36}\\)<br>14 दिनों (7 जोड़े) में = \\(\\frac{35}{36}\\), शेष \\(\\frac{1}{36}\\)<br>15वें दिन A कार्य करता है: A प्रतिदिन \\(\\frac{1}{9}\\) करता है, अतः शेष कार्य में \\(\\frac{1/36}{1/9} = \\frac{1}{4}\\) दिन लगेगा<br>कुल = \\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) दिन = \\(\\boxed{14\\frac{1}{4}}\\) दिन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(14\\frac{1}{4}\\) दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000074944","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\tan\\theta_1 \\cdot \\tan\\theta_2 = 2\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{\\cos(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)}{\\cos(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\tan\\theta_1 \\cdot \\tan\\theta_2 = 2\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{\\cos(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)}{\\cos(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"-3"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"-4"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Dividing numerator and denominator by \\(\\cos\\theta_1\\cos\\theta_2\\):<br>\\(\\frac{\\cos(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)}{\\cos(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)} = \\frac{1 + \\tan\\theta_1\\tan\\theta_2}{1 - \\tan\\theta_1\\tan\\theta_2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1 + 2}{1 - 2} = \\boxed{-3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): -3.</b>","hi":"अंश और हर दोनों को \\(\\cos\\theta_1\\cos\\theta_2\\) से भाग देने पर:<br>\\(\\frac{\\cos(\\theta_1-\\theta_2)}{\\cos(\\theta_1+\\theta_2)} = \\frac{1 + \\tan\\theta_1\\tan\\theta_2}{1 - \\tan\\theta_1\\tan\\theta_2}\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1 + 2}{1 - 2} = \\boxed{-3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): -3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000074945","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}+20}{\\sqrt{5}}\\). [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{5} = 2.236\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5}+20}{\\sqrt{5}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4.765"},"2":{"en":"8.245"},"3":{"en":"13.944"},"4":{"en":"16.786"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} + 20}{\\sqrt{5}} = 5 + \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br>\\(= 5 + 4\\sqrt{5} = 5 + 4 \\times 2.236\\)<br>\\(= 5 + 8.944 = \\boxed{13.944}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 13.944.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{5} + 20}{\\sqrt{5}} = 5 + \\frac{20}{\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br>\\(= 5 + 4\\sqrt{5} = 5 + 4 \\times 2.236\\)<br>\\(= 5 + 8.944 = \\boxed{13.944}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 13.944 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000074946","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The hemispherical dome of a building is to be painted. If the circumference of its base is 44 m, determine the cost of painting the dome at a rate of ₹25 per square meter. (Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक भवन के अर्धगोलाकार गुंबद पर पुताई करनी है। यदि उसके आधार की परिधि 44 m है, तो ₹25 प्रति वर्ग मीटर की दर से गुंबद पर पुताई की लागत ज्ञात कीजिए। (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹7700"},"2":{"en":"₹6500"},"3":{"en":"₹8800"},"4":{"en":"₹6870"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"158\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 158\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 106A80 26 0 0 0 186 106M186 106A80 80 0 0 0 26 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 106A80 26 0 0 1 186 106M106 106L186 106\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"11\">r = 7 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(2\\pi r = 44 \\Rightarrow 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} r = 44 \\Rightarrow r = 7\\) m<br>Curved surface area = \\(2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 308\\) m²<br>Cost = ₹\\(308 \\times 25 = \\boxed{7700}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): ₹7700.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"158\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 158\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 106A80 26 0 0 0 186 106M186 106A80 80 0 0 0 26 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 106A80 26 0 0 1 186 106M106 106L186 106\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"11\">r = 7 m</text></g></svg><br>\\(2\\pi r = 44 \\Rightarrow 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} r = 44 \\Rightarrow r = 7\\) m<br>वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल = \\(2\\pi r^2 = 2 \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 49 = 308\\) m²<br>लागत = ₹\\(308 \\times 25 = \\boxed{7700}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): ₹7700 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000074947","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle of radius 15 cm, two equal parallel chords lie on opposite sides of the centre. The distance between the chords is 18 cm. Find the length of each chord. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"15 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त में दो बराबर समांतर जीवाएँ केंद्र के विपरीत दिशाओं में स्थित हैं। जीवाओं के बीच की दूरी 18 cm है। प्रत्येक जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"12 cm"},"3":{"en":"16 cm"},"4":{"en":"24 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 62L188 62M44 170L188 170M122 62L122 68L116 68M122 170L122 164L116 164M116 116L188 62\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 62L116 170\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"118\">O</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"100\">15</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"58\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"58\">B</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">D</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">9</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">9</text></g></svg><br>Equal chords are equidistant from the centre, so each is \\(\\frac{18}{2} = 9\\) cm from the centre.<br>Half chord = \\(\\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{225 - 81} = 12\\) cm<br>Length of each chord = \\(2 \\times 12 = \\boxed{24}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 24 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 62L188 62M44 170L188 170M122 62L122 68L116 68M122 170L122 164L116 164M116 116L188 62\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 62L116 170\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"118\">O</text><text x=\"157\" y=\"100\">15</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"58\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"58\">B</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">D</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">9</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">9</text></g></svg><br>बराबर जीवाएँ केंद्र से समान दूरी पर होती हैं, अतः प्रत्येक केंद्र से \\(\\frac{18}{2} = 9\\) cm दूर है।<br>आधी जीवा = \\(\\sqrt{15^2 - 9^2} = \\sqrt{225 - 81} = 12\\) cm<br>प्रत्येक जीवा की लंबाई = \\(2 \\times 12 = \\boxed{24}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 24 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000074948","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Triangle PQR is inscribed in a circle. A tangent is drawn at P parallel to QR. If triangle PQR is equilateral (PQ = QR = PR), what is the angle ∠QPR between chord PQ and chord PR as seen from P? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"त्रिभुज PQR एक वृत्त में अंतर्निहित है। P पर QR के समांतर एक स्पर्श रेखा खींची जाती है। यदि त्रिभुज PQR समबाहु है (PQ = QR = PR), तो P से देखने पर जीवा PQ और जीवा PR के बीच का कोण ∠QPR क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20°"},"2":{"en":"30°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"90°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In an equilateral triangle each interior angle is \\(\\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\\)<br>So the angle between chords PQ and PR at P is<br>\\(\\angle QPR = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60°.</b>","hi":"समबाहु त्रिभुज का प्रत्येक आंतरिक कोण \\(\\frac{180^\\circ}{3} = 60^\\circ\\) होता है<br>अतः P पर जीवाओं PQ और PR के बीच का कोण<br>\\(\\angle QPR = \\boxed{60^\\circ}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000074949","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"The angles of a pentagon are in the ratio 1 : 2 : 3 : 4 : 5. What is the second largest angle in radians? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पंचभुज के कोण 1 : 2 : 3 : 4 : 5 के अनुपात में हैं। रेडियन में दूसरा सबसे बड़ा कोण क्या है? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\) रेडियन"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{5}\\) रेडियन"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{5}\\) रेडियन"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\) रेडियन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Sum of the interior angles of a pentagon = \\((5 - 2) \\times 180^\\circ = 540^\\circ\\)<br>\\(x + 2x + 3x + 4x + 5x = 15x = 540^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = 36^\\circ\\)<br>Second largest angle = \\(4x = 144^\\circ\\)<br>In radians: \\(144 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} = \\boxed{\\frac{4\\pi}{5}}\\) radians<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\) radians.</b>","hi":"पंचभुज के आंतरिक कोणों का योग = \\((5 - 2) \\times 180^\\circ = 540^\\circ\\)<br>\\(x + 2x + 3x + 4x + 5x = 15x = 540^\\circ \\Rightarrow x = 36^\\circ\\)<br>दूसरा सबसे बड़ा कोण = \\(4x = 144^\\circ\\)<br>रेडियन में: \\(144 \\times \\frac{\\pi}{180} = \\boxed{\\frac{4\\pi}{5}}\\) रेडियन<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{4\\pi}{5}\\) रेडियन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000074950","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Two workers, Moti and Nandu, are building a brick wall that requires exactly 120 bricks. Moti lays 15 bricks per hour, but after every hour he works, he takes a 1-hour break. Nandu works continuously and lays 10 bricks per hour. Both start working together at the same time. However, a site hazard knocks down 5 bricks at the exact end of every hour. How much time will it take to complete laying 120 bricks for the very first time? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो श्रमिक, मोती और नंदू, एक ईंट की दीवार बना रहे हैं जिसके लिए ठीक 120 ईंटें चाहिए। मोती प्रति घंटे 15 ईंटें लगाता है, परंतु प्रत्येक एक घंटे कार्य के बाद 1 घंटे का विश्राम लेता है। नंदू लगातार कार्य करता है और प्रति घंटे 10 ईंटें लगाता है। दोनों एक साथ कार्य शुरू करते हैं। परंतु प्रत्येक घंटे के ठीक अंत में एक साइट खतरा 5 ईंटें गिरा देता है। ठीक 120 ईंटें पहली बार पूरी होने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"7 hrs 52 mins","hi":"7 घंटे 52 मिनट"},"2":{"en":"8 hrs 32 mins","hi":"8 घंटे 32 मिनट"},"3":{"en":"8 hrs 48 mins","hi":"8 घंटे 48 मिनट"},"4":{"en":"9 hrs 28 mins","hi":"9 घंटे 28 मिनट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In a 2-hour cycle Moti works 1 hour and rests 1 hour, while Nandu works both hours; the hazard strikes twice.<br>Bricks per 2-hour cycle = \\(15 + 2 \\times 10 - 2 \\times 5 = 25\\)<br>After 8 hours (4 cycles) = \\(4 \\times 25 = 100\\) bricks<br>In hour 9 Moti works, so the rate is \\(15 + 10 = 25\\) bricks/hour; the remaining 20 bricks take \\(\\frac{20}{25}\\) h = 48 min<br>Total = \\(8\\) h \\(48\\) min = \\boxed{8\\ \\text{hrs}\\ 48\\ \\text{mins}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 8 hrs 48 mins.</b>","hi":"2 घंटे के चक्र में मोती 1 घंटा कार्य करता है और 1 घंटा विश्राम लेता है, जबकि नंदू दोनों घंटे कार्य करता है; खतरा दो बार होता है।<br>प्रति 2 घंटे के चक्र में ईंटें = \\(15 + 2 \\times 10 - 2 \\times 5 = 25\\)<br>8 घंटे (4 चक्र) बाद = \\(4 \\times 25 = 100\\) ईंटें<br>9वें घंटे में मोती कार्य करता है, अतः दर \\(15 + 10 = 25\\) ईंटें/घंटा; शेष 20 ईंटों में \\(\\frac{20}{25}\\) घंटा = 48 मिनट लगेंगे<br>कुल = \\(8\\) घंटे \\(48\\) मिनट = \\boxed{8\\ \\text{घंटे}\\ 48\\ \\text{मिनट}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 8 घंटे 48 मिनट है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000074951","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a right triangle ABC with ∠B = 90°, simplify: \\(\\frac{\\sin A+\\cos C}{\\sin C+\\cos A}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"∠B = 90° वाले समकोण त्रिभुज ABC में सरल कीजिए: \\(\\frac{\\sin A+\\cos C}{\\sin C+\\cos A}\\) [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"cot A"},"2":{"en":"tan A"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"sin A"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(A + C = 90^\\circ\\), so \\(\\cos C = \\sin A\\) and \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>Expression = \\(\\frac{\\sin A + \\sin A}{\\cos A + \\cos A} = \\frac{2\\sin A}{2\\cos A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\tan A}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): tan A.</b>","hi":"\\(A + C = 90^\\circ\\), अतः \\(\\cos C = \\sin A\\) और \\(\\sin C = \\cos A\\)<br>व्यंजक = \\(\\frac{\\sin A + \\sin A}{\\cos A + \\cos A} = \\frac{2\\sin A}{2\\cos A}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\tan A}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): tan A है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000074952","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Consider the statement: 99.8² = 10000 − K + 0.04. To make this statement mathematically true, what must be the value of K? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन पर विचार कीजिए: 99.8² = 10000 − K + 0.04। इस कथन को गणितीय रूप से सत्य बनाने के लिए K का मान क्या होना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0.4"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"40"},"4":{"en":"400"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(99.8^2 = (100 - 0.2)^2 = 10000 - 2 \\times 100 \\times 0.2 + 0.04\\)<br>\\(= 10000 - 40 + 0.04 = 9960.04\\)<br>Comparing with \\(10000 - K + 0.04\\), we get \\(K = \\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 40.</b>","hi":"\\(99.8^2 = (100 - 0.2)^2 = 10000 - 2 \\times 100 \\times 0.2 + 0.04\\)<br>\\(= 10000 - 40 + 0.04 = 9960.04\\)<br>\\(10000 - K + 0.04\\) से तुलना करने पर, \\(K = \\boxed{40}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 40 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000074953","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"A water tank has three pipes attached to it. Pipe 1 and Pipe 2 are inlet pipes that fill the tank in 5/2 hours and 10/3 hours respectively. Pipe 3 is an outlet pipe that empties the full tank in 5 hours. If all three pipes are opened together, how long will it take to fill the empty tank? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पानी की टंकी से तीन पाइप जुड़े हैं। पाइप 1 और पाइप 2 भरने वाले पाइप हैं जो टंकी को क्रमशः 5/2 घंटे और 10/3 घंटे में भरते हैं। पाइप 3 निकास पाइप है जो भरी टंकी को 5 घंटे में खाली करता है। यदि तीनों पाइप एक साथ खोल दिए जाएँ, तो खाली टंकी भरने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(1\\frac{1}{2}\\) hours","hi":"\\(1\\frac{1}{2}\\) घंटे"},"2":{"en":"\\(2\\frac{1}{2}\\) hours","hi":"\\(2\\frac{1}{2}\\) घंटे"},"3":{"en":"2 hours","hi":"2 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"3 hours","hi":"3 घंटे"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rates: pipe 1 = \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\), pipe 2 = \\(\\frac{3}{10}\\), outlet = \\(-\\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>Net rate = \\(\\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{3}{10} - \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{4 + 3 - 2}{10} = \\frac{5}{10} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>Time = \\(\\boxed{2}\\) hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 2 hours.</b>","hi":"दरें: पाइप 1 = \\(\\frac{2}{5}\\), पाइप 2 = \\(\\frac{3}{10}\\), निकास = \\(-\\frac{1}{5}\\)<br>शुद्ध दर = \\(\\frac{2}{5} + \\frac{3}{10} - \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{4 + 3 - 2}{10} = \\frac{5}{10} = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>समय = \\(\\boxed{2}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 2 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000074954","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"For a vertical tower of height h standing on horizontal ground, the angle of elevation from a point on the ground at a horizontal distance d from its base is θ. If the height of the tower is increased by 20% and then further increased by 25%, while the distance of the observer is first decreased by 20% and then increased by 25%, then the new angle of elevation θ′ satisfies: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"क्षैतिज भूमि पर खड़े h ऊँचाई वाले ऊर्ध्वाधर मीनार के लिए, उसके आधार से d क्षैतिज दूरी पर स्थित भूमि के बिंदु से उन्नयन कोण θ है। यदि मीनार की ऊँचाई पहले 20% बढ़ाई जाए और फिर 25% और बढ़ाई जाए, तथा प्रेक्षक की दूरी पहले 20% घटाई जाए और फिर 25% बढ़ाई जाए, तो नया उन्नयन कोण θ′ संतुष्ट करता है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{15}{8}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{5}{4}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\tan\\theta\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"223\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"-11 0 223 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L186 186M26 186L26 79M186 186L26 79M34 186L34 178L26 178M152 186A34 34 0 0 1 158 167M126 186A60 60 0 0 1 144 144\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 79L26 26M186 186L26 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"142\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"11\">θ</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11\">θ′</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"137\">h</text><text x=\"5\" y=\"57\">0.5h</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"202\">d</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"197\">P</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"197\">B</text></g></svg><br>New height = \\(h \\times 1.2 \\times 1.25 = 1.5h\\)<br>New distance = \\(d \\times 0.8 \\times 1.25 = d\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\frac{1.5h}{d} = 1.5\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\), i.e. \\(\\boxed{\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"223\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"-11 0 223 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 186L186 186M26 186L26 79M186 186L26 79M34 186L34 178L26 178M152 186A34 34 0 0 1 158 167M126 186A60 60 0 0 1 144 144\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 79L26 26M186 186L26 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"142\" y=\"177\" font-size=\"11\">θ</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"142\" font-size=\"11\">θ′</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"137\">h</text><text x=\"5\" y=\"57\">0.5h</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"202\">d</text><text x=\"194\" y=\"197\">P</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"197\">B</text></g></svg><br>नई ऊँचाई = \\(h \\times 1.2 \\times 1.25 = 1.5h\\)<br>नई दूरी = \\(d \\times 0.8 \\times 1.25 = d\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\frac{1.5h}{d} = 1.5\\tan\\theta\\)<br>\\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\), अर्थात् \\(\\boxed{\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\tan\\theta' = \\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\tan\\theta\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000074955","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"The transverse common tangents to two completely separate coplanar circles, having radii r₁ and r₂ respectively, intersect at a point on the line segment joining their centers. This point divides the line segment from the center of the first circle to the center of the second circle in the ratio: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दो पूर्णतः अलग समतलीय वृत्तों, जिनकी त्रिज्याएँ क्रमशः r₁ और r₂ हैं, की तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ उनके केंद्रों को मिलाने वाले रेखाखंड पर एक बिंदु पर प्रतिच्छेद करती हैं। यह बिंदु पहले वृत्त के केंद्र से दूसरे वृत्त के केंद्र तक के रेखाखंड को किस अनुपात में विभाजित करता है: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(r_1 : r_2\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\((r_1 + r_2) : r_1\\)"},"3":{"en":"1 : 1"},"4":{"en":"\\((r_1 + r_2) : (r_1 - r_2)\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"302\" height=\"156\" viewBox=\"0 0 302 156\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M82 26L245 120M76 80L101 37M243 80L226 109M98 42L103 45L106 40M229 104L224 101L221 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M76 80L243 80\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"80\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"243\" cy=\"80\" r=\"33\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"243\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"176\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"73\" y=\"92\">A</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"92\">B</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"34\">P</text><text x=\"228\" y=\"120\">Q</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"75\">X</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"68\">r₁</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"93\">r₂</text></g></svg><br>The two transverse tangents and the line of centres form two similar right triangles with the radii as corresponding sides.<br>So the intersection point divides the line of centres internally in the ratio of the radii:<br>\\(\\boxed{r_1 : r_2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(r_1 : r_2\\).</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"302\" height=\"156\" viewBox=\"0 0 302 156\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M82 26L245 120M76 80L101 37M243 80L226 109M98 42L103 45L106 40M229 104L224 101L221 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M76 80L243 80\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"80\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"243\" cy=\"80\" r=\"33\"/><circle cx=\"76\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"243\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><circle cx=\"176\" cy=\"80\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"73\" y=\"92\">A</text><text x=\"245\" y=\"92\">B</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"34\">P</text><text x=\"228\" y=\"120\">Q</text><text x=\"184\" y=\"75\">X</text><text x=\"97\" y=\"68\">r₁</text><text x=\"225\" y=\"93\">r₂</text></g></svg><br>दोनों तिर्यक स्पर्श रेखाएँ और केंद्र-रेखा दो समरूप समकोण त्रिभुज बनाती हैं जिनमें त्रिज्याएँ संगत भुजाएँ हैं।<br>अतः प्रतिच्छेद बिंदु केंद्र-रेखा को त्रिज्याओं के अनुपात में अंतः विभाजित करता है:<br>\\(\\boxed{r_1 : r_2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(r_1 : r_2\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000074956","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems for over 160 million years, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination. Emerging during the Triassic Period approximately 230 million years ago, dinosaurs diversified rapidly, exploiting ecological niches ranging from apex predation to herbivorous grazing.<br><br>Paleontological evidence reveals that dinosaurs were not monolithic; they represented an extraordinary array of morphologies, behaviours, and metabolic strategies. Contrary to the once-prevailing image of sluggish, cold-blooded reptiles, current research suggests that many species, particularly theropods, exhibited endothermic traits and dynamic activity levels. Feathers, once considered exclusive to modern birds, have been identified in numerous non-avian dinosaur fossils, suggesting evolutionary continuity rather than abrupt transformation.<br><br>The Cretaceous-Palaeogene (K-Pg.) extinction event, approximately 66 million years ago, precipitated the demise of non-avian dinosaurs, plausibly triggered by an asteroid impact combined with extensive volcanic activity. This cataclysmic shift not only eradicated dominant dinosaurian lineages but also catalysed mammalian diversification, reshaping evolutionary trajectories.<br><br>Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analysing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist. Questions concerning precise dinosaurian physiology, social behaviour, and even the nuances of their extinction dynamics remain partially speculative. Moreover, the fossil record itself is inherently incomplete, biased toward preservation-friendly environments, thereby skewing interpretations.<br><br>Ultimately, the study of dinosaurs transcends mere historical reconstruction; it probes the intricate processes of evolution, adaptation, and extinction—processes that remain profoundly relevant in an era of accelerating environmental change.<br><br><br>In the sentence “Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination,” what is the grammatical function of the clause “that dominated terrestrial ecosystems”? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Adverbial Clause"},"2":{"en":"Noun Clause"},"3":{"en":"Relative Clause"},"4":{"en":"Prepositional Clause"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A relative clause modifies a noun and begins with a relative pronoun.</b><br>“That dominated terrestrial ecosystems” modifies “archosaurs.”<br>“That” refers to the archosaurs and acts as the clause’s subject.<br>It is not a noun, adverbial or prepositional clause.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Relative Clause.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000074957","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems for over 160 million years, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination. Emerging during the Triassic Period approximately 230 million years ago, dinosaurs diversified rapidly, exploiting ecological niches ranging from apex predation to herbivorous grazing.<br><br>Paleontological evidence reveals that dinosaurs were not monolithic; they represented an extraordinary array of morphologies, behaviours, and metabolic strategies. Contrary to the once-prevailing image of sluggish, cold-blooded reptiles, current research suggests that many species, particularly theropods, exhibited endothermic traits and dynamic activity levels. Feathers, once considered exclusive to modern birds, have been identified in numerous non-avian dinosaur fossils, suggesting evolutionary continuity rather than abrupt transformation.<br><br>The Cretaceous-Palaeogene (K-Pg.) extinction event, approximately 66 million years ago, precipitated the demise of non-avian dinosaurs, plausibly triggered by an asteroid impact combined with extensive volcanic activity. This cataclysmic shift not only eradicated dominant dinosaurian lineages but also catalysed mammalian diversification, reshaping evolutionary trajectories.<br><br>Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analysing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist. Questions concerning precise dinosaurian physiology, social behaviour, and even the nuances of their extinction dynamics remain partially speculative. Moreover, the fossil record itself is inherently incomplete, biased toward preservation-friendly environments, thereby skewing interpretations.<br><br>Ultimately, the study of dinosaurs transcends mere historical reconstruction; it probes the intricate processes of evolution, adaptation, and extinction—processes that remain profoundly relevant in an era of accelerating environmental change.<br><br><br>The word “precipitated” most nearly means: [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Delayed"},"2":{"en":"Caused suddenly"},"3":{"en":"Questioned"},"4":{"en":"Neutralized"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Precipitate (तेज़ी से घटित करना) = cause something to happen suddenly.</b><br>The extinction event brought about the demise of non-avian dinosaurs.<br>Delayed means postponed, questioned means challenged.<br>Neutralized means counteracted.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Caused suddenly.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000074958","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems for over 160 million years, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination. Emerging during the Triassic Period approximately 230 million years ago, dinosaurs diversified rapidly, exploiting ecological niches ranging from apex predation to herbivorous grazing.<br><br>Paleontological evidence reveals that dinosaurs were not monolithic; they represented an extraordinary array of morphologies, behaviours, and metabolic strategies. Contrary to the once-prevailing image of sluggish, cold-blooded reptiles, current research suggests that many species, particularly theropods, exhibited endothermic traits and dynamic activity levels. Feathers, once considered exclusive to modern birds, have been identified in numerous non-avian dinosaur fossils, suggesting evolutionary continuity rather than abrupt transformation.<br><br>The Cretaceous-Palaeogene (K-Pg.) extinction event, approximately 66 million years ago, precipitated the demise of non-avian dinosaurs, plausibly triggered by an asteroid impact combined with extensive volcanic activity. This cataclysmic shift not only eradicated dominant dinosaurian lineages but also catalysed mammalian diversification, reshaping evolutionary trajectories.<br><br>Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analysing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist. Questions concerning precise dinosaurian physiology, social behaviour, and even the nuances of their extinction dynamics remain partially speculative. Moreover, the fossil record itself is inherently incomplete, biased toward preservation-friendly environments, thereby skewing interpretations.<br><br>Ultimately, the study of dinosaurs transcends mere historical reconstruction; it probes the intricate processes of evolution, adaptation, and extinction—processes that remain profoundly relevant in an era of accelerating environmental change.<br><br><br>Choose the best synonym for “enigma” as used in the passage. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Certainty"},"2":{"en":"Mystery"},"3":{"en":"Debate"},"4":{"en":"Explanation"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Enigma (रहस्य) = something mysterious or difficult to understand.</b><br>The passage says critical enigmas persist despite technological advances.<br>“Mystery” is the closest synonym.<br>Certainty and explanation are opposite in this context; debate is not exact.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Mystery.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000074959","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems for over 160 million years, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination. Emerging during the Triassic Period approximately 230 million years ago, dinosaurs diversified rapidly, exploiting ecological niches ranging from apex predation to herbivorous grazing.<br><br>Paleontological evidence reveals that dinosaurs were not monolithic; they represented an extraordinary array of morphologies, behaviours, and metabolic strategies. Contrary to the once-prevailing image of sluggish, cold-blooded reptiles, current research suggests that many species, particularly theropods, exhibited endothermic traits and dynamic activity levels. Feathers, once considered exclusive to modern birds, have been identified in numerous non-avian dinosaur fossils, suggesting evolutionary continuity rather than abrupt transformation.<br><br>The Cretaceous-Palaeogene (K-Pg.) extinction event, approximately 66 million years ago, precipitated the demise of non-avian dinosaurs, plausibly triggered by an asteroid impact combined with extensive volcanic activity. This cataclysmic shift not only eradicated dominant dinosaurian lineages but also catalysed mammalian diversification, reshaping evolutionary trajectories.<br><br>Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analysing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist. Questions concerning precise dinosaurian physiology, social behaviour, and even the nuances of their extinction dynamics remain partially speculative. Moreover, the fossil record itself is inherently incomplete, biased toward preservation-friendly environments, thereby skewing interpretations.<br><br>Ultimately, the study of dinosaurs transcends mere historical reconstruction; it probes the intricate processes of evolution, adaptation, and extinction—processes that remain profoundly relevant in an era of accelerating environmental change.<br><br><br>According to the passage, why is the study of dinosaurs considered relevant today? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It helps predict asteroid impacts."},"2":{"en":"It enhances fossil preservation techniques."},"3":{"en":"It reveals processes vital for understanding current environmental changes."},"4":{"en":"It proves that mammals evolved before dinosaurs."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Text evidence: Evolution, adaptation and extinction remain relevant amid accelerating environmental change.</b><br>Dinosaur research illuminates these long-term biological processes.<br>It is not presented as predicting impacts or proving mammals evolved first.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): It reveals processes vital for understanding current environmental changes.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000074960","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>Dinosaurs, the magnificent archosaurs that dominated terrestrial ecosystems for over 160 million years, continue to captivate both scientific inquiry and popular imagination. Emerging during the Triassic Period approximately 230 million years ago, dinosaurs diversified rapidly, exploiting ecological niches ranging from apex predation to herbivorous grazing.<br><br>Paleontological evidence reveals that dinosaurs were not monolithic; they represented an extraordinary array of morphologies, behaviours, and metabolic strategies. Contrary to the once-prevailing image of sluggish, cold-blooded reptiles, current research suggests that many species, particularly theropods, exhibited endothermic traits and dynamic activity levels. Feathers, once considered exclusive to modern birds, have been identified in numerous non-avian dinosaur fossils, suggesting evolutionary continuity rather than abrupt transformation.<br><br>The Cretaceous-Palaeogene (K-Pg.) extinction event, approximately 66 million years ago, precipitated the demise of non-avian dinosaurs, plausibly triggered by an asteroid impact combined with extensive volcanic activity. This cataclysmic shift not only eradicated dominant dinosaurian lineages but also catalysed mammalian diversification, reshaping evolutionary trajectories.<br><br>Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analysing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist. Questions concerning precise dinosaurian physiology, social behaviour, and even the nuances of their extinction dynamics remain partially speculative. Moreover, the fossil record itself is inherently incomplete, biased toward preservation-friendly environments, thereby skewing interpretations.<br><br>Ultimately, the study of dinosaurs transcends mere historical reconstruction; it probes the intricate processes of evolution, adaptation, and extinction—processes that remain profoundly relevant in an era of accelerating environmental change.<br><br><br>In the sentence “Yet, despite monumental advances in technology—from CT-scanning fossilized bones to analyzing isotopic signatures—critical enigmas persist,” what is the function of the phrase “despite monumental advances in technology”? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Main Clause"},"2":{"en":"Adjective phrase"},"3":{"en":"Adverbial phrase of contrast"},"4":{"en":"Noun phrase functioning as subject"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Despite + noun phrase” introduces a concessive contrast.</b><br>Technological advances contrast with the persistence of critical mysteries.<br>The phrase modifies the whole main clause rather than a single noun.<br>It is therefore an adverbial phrase of contrast.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Adverbial phrase of contrast.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000074961","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br>The diplomat spoke in a ___ manner, avoiding any inflammatory remarks. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"circumspect"},"2":{"en":"circumpect"},"3":{"en":"circumspeckt"},"4":{"en":"circumspace"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Circumspect (सावधान) = cautious and discreet.</b><br>The correct spelling is “circumspect.”<br><b>Circumpect</b> omits “s”; <b>circumspeckt</b> inserts “k.”<br><b>Circumspace</b> is not the required word.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): circumspect.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000074962","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the appropriate preposition.<br>The agreement remained ___ abeyance until further notice. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"at"},"2":{"en":"on"},"3":{"en":"under"},"4":{"en":"in"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “In abeyance” means temporarily suspended.</b><br>The agreement remained inactive until further notice.<br>“At,” “on” and “under” do not form the standard phrase.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): in.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000074963","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>With the rapid expansion of the cryptocurrency market,<br>P. prompting governments to establish strict regulatory frameworks,<br>Q. while investors faced heightened market volatility due to regulatory uncertainties<br>R. concerns over financial stability and illicit transactions escalated,<br>S. leading to increased scrutiny on decentralized finance platforms, [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRSQ"},"2":{"en":"RPSQ"},"3":{"en":"SQPR"},"4":{"en":"QPRS"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPSQ</b><br>R states the escalation of concerns.<br>P gives the governmental response, and S adds scrutiny of decentralized platforms.<br>Q concludes with investors’ volatility amid uncertainty.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RPSQ.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000074964","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br>The prestigious innovation award<br>P. for developing a revolutionary energy-efficient device<br>Q. that significantly reduces carbon emissions<br>R. was presented to the young engineer<br>S. at an international technology summit [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SQPR"},"2":{"en":"RPQS"},"3":{"en":"PSRQ"},"4":{"en":"QPSR"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RPQS</b><br>R supplies the main predicate and recipient.<br>P explains the engineer’s achievement.<br>Q describes the device’s emissions benefit, and S gives the summit setting.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): RPQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000074965","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the sentence by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br>Neither the manager nor his assistants ___ prepared for the sudden audit. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Was"},"2":{"en":"were"},"3":{"en":"is"},"4":{"en":"be"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: With “neither … nor,” the verb agrees with the nearer subject.</b><br>The nearer subject “assistants” is plural.<br>“Were prepared” also fits the past context of the sudden audit.<br>The other options do not provide plural past agreement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): were.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000074966","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br>We arrived at <b>a</b> Himalayas before sunrise. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Himalayas"},"2":{"en":"sunrise"},"3":{"en":"arrived"},"4":{"en":"a"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Mountain ranges take the definite article “the.”</b><br>Correct sentence: “We arrived at <b>the</b> Himalayas before sunrise.”<br>The indefinite article “a” is incorrect.<br>The other words are correct.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): a.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000074967","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence using the correct phrasal verb of the underlined words.<br>He tried to <b>take away</b> a new business after his retirement. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"take in"},"2":{"en":"take over"},"3":{"en":"take up"},"4":{"en":"take out"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Take up (आरंभ करना) = start a new activity or venture.</b><br>He started a new business after retirement.<br><b>Take in</b> = absorb; <b>take over</b> = assume control<br><b>Take out</b> = remove<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): take up.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000074968","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br>Yesterday, in a collision between a truck and a car, he had a <b>close shave</b>. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A minor injury"},"2":{"en":"A lucky escape"},"3":{"en":"A serious accident"},"4":{"en":"A smooth journey"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>A close shave (बाल-बाल बचना) = a narrow or lucky escape.</b><br>He narrowly avoided serious harm in the collision.<br>Minor injury and serious accident are not the idiom’s meaning.<br>A smooth journey contradicts the collision.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): A lucky escape.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000074969","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom “let bygones be bygones” mean? [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To forget past grievances and forgive"},"2":{"en":"To hold onto past grudges"},"3":{"en":"To revisit old conflicts frequently"},"4":{"en":"To seek revenge for past wrongs"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Let bygones be bygones (बीती बातें भुलाना) = forgive past offences.</b><br>Example: “They decided to let bygones be bygones and renew their friendship.”<br>Grudges, conflict and revenge are opposite responses.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To forget past grievances and forgive.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000074970","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. The concrete operational stage marks the development of logical thinking and understanding of conservation.<br>2. In the sensorimotor stage, infants learn through sensory experiences and motor actions, developing object permanence.<br>3. In the preoperational stage, children begin using symbols and language but still lack logical reasoning abilities.<br>4. In the formal operational stage, adolescents develop the ability to think abstractly and hypothetically.<br>5. Jean Piaget proposed that cognitive development occurs in four distinct stages. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-3-5-4-2"},"2":{"en":"2-5-1-4-3"},"3":{"en":"5-2-3-1-4"},"4":{"en":"3-1-2-4-5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 5-2-3-1-4</b><br>Sentence 5 introduces Piaget’s four stages.<br>The remaining sentences follow developmental order: sensorimotor, preoperational, concrete operational, formal operational.<br>This preserves both chronology and logic.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5-2-3-1-4.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000074971","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?<br>1. The therapist and client work together to replace maladaptive thinking with healthier, more rational thought processes.<br>2. It helps individuals identify and challenge negative thought patterns that lead to emotional distress.<br>3. The goal is to teach clients coping strategies to manage their emotions and behaviours effectively.<br>4. Cognitive Behavioral Therapy focuses on the relationship between thoughts, feelings and behaviours.<br>5. This method has been shown to be effective in treating a wide range of mental health conditions, including anxiety and depression. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-2-5-4-1"},"2":{"en":"2-4-5-1-3"},"3":{"en":"3-1-4-2-5"},"4":{"en":"4-2-1-3-5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-2-1-3-5</b><br>Sentence 4 introduces CBT, and sentence 2 explains its identification of negative thoughts.<br>Sentence 1 describes replacement with healthier thinking, followed by coping strategies in 3.<br>Sentence 5 concludes with evidence of effectiveness.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4-2-1-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000074972","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>TACIT</b> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Explicit"},"2":{"en":"Silent"},"3":{"en":"Implied"},"4":{"en":"Declared"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Tacit (अकथित) = understood without being openly stated.</b><br><b>Explicit (स्पष्ट)</b> = clearly stated<br><b>Silent (मौन)</b> = without speech<br><b>Implied (अंतर्निहित)</b> = suggested but not stated ✔<br><b>Declared (घोषित)</b> = announced; synonyms: implicit, unspoken.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Implied.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000074973","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Lament</b> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Celebrate"},"2":{"en":"Mourn"},"3":{"en":"Wail"},"4":{"en":"Grieve"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Lament (विलाप करना) = express sorrow.</b><br><b>Celebrate (जश्न मनाना)</b> = express joy ✔<br><b>Mourn (शोक करना)</b> = grieve<br><b>Wail (विलाप करना)</b> = cry loudly; <b>grieve (दुःखी होना)</b> = sorrow.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Celebrate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000074974","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>PUGNACIOUS</b> [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Serene"},"2":{"en":"Calm"},"3":{"en":"Docile"},"4":{"en":"Combative"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Pugnacious (झगड़ालू) = eager to fight.</b><br><b>Serene (शांत)</b> = peaceful<br><b>Calm (शांत)</b> = untroubled<br><b>Docile (विनम्र)</b> = submissive<br><b>Combative (युद्धप्रिय)</b> = ready to fight ✔<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Combative.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000074975","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Spot the correct spelling of a term for “human-centered thinking”. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Anthropocentric"},"2":{"en":"Anthropocentrix"},"3":{"en":"Anthropacentric"},"4":{"en":"Anthropocentik"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Anthropocentric (मानव-केंद्रित) = regarding humans as central.</b><br>The correct spelling is “anthropocentric.”<br><b>Anthropocentrix</b> changes the ending to “x.”<br><b>Anthropacentric</b> inserts “a”; <b>Anthropocentik</b> uses “k.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Anthropocentric.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000074976","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct one-word substitute for: “A person who studies the origin of words”. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lexicographer"},"2":{"en":"Philologist"},"3":{"en":"Etymologist"},"4":{"en":"Paleographer"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Etymologist (शब्दोत्पत्ति-विशेषज्ञ) = one who studies word origins.</b><br><b>Lexicographer (कोशकार)</b> = dictionary compiler<br><b>Philologist (भाषाविद)</b> = language scholar<br><b>Paleographer (पुरालेख-विशेषज्ञ)</b> = scholar of ancient writing<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Etymologist.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000074977","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Change the following from active to passive:<br>Engineers are conducting tests. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tests were conducted by engineers."},"2":{"en":"Tests have been conducted by engineers."},"3":{"en":"Tests are being conducted by engineers."},"4":{"en":"Tests had been conducted by engineers."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present continuous passive = am/is/are being + past participle.</b><br>The plural object “tests” takes “are being conducted.”<br>The agent “engineers” is retained.<br>The other options change the tense.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Tests are being conducted by engineers.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000074978","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Select the sentence containing the homonym of the highlighted word:<br>The <b>content</b> of the speech was thought-provoking. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They found new content in the document."},"2":{"en":"The artist uploaded fresh content daily."},"3":{"en":"His content appeared in the magazine."},"4":{"en":"She was content with the outcome."}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Content = material contained in something; content = satisfied.</b><br>The original uses the noun meaning subject matter.<br>Option D uses the adjective meaning satisfied.<br>The other options retain the material meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): She was content with the outcome.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000074979","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He <b>is working hardly</b> to succeed. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"works hardly"},"2":{"en":"is working hard"},"3":{"en":"has been hardly working"},"4":{"en":"is hard working"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Hard” means with effort; “hardly” means almost not.</b><br>Correct sentence: “He <b>is working hard</b> to succeed.”<br>The present continuous is appropriate for ongoing effort.<br>The other options retain “hardly” or use a compound adjective incorrectly.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): is working hard.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000074980","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The historian spent years attempting to establish the <b>verity</b> of the ancient scrolls. [SSC CGL 24/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Authenticity"},"2":{"en":"Probity"},"3":{"en":"Mendacity"},"4":{"en":"Rectitude"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Verity (सत्यता) = truthfulness or truth.</b><br><b>Authenticity (प्रामाणिकता)</b> = genuineness<br><b>Probity (सत्यनिष्ठा)</b> = integrity<br><b>Mendacity (झूठ)</b> = dishonesty ✔<br><b>Rectitude (नेकी)</b> = moral correctness<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Mendacity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};